{"_id":"wmMark0000000001","name":"Tempered Construction — Blacksmithing — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-universal-tempered-construction"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000001","name":"Tempered Construction","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tempered Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Armor or shield gains +50% of its pre-Mark maximum item HP and +Core Tier Hardness. This improves the item, not its wearer&#39;s HP. Durability bonuses add against the same pre-Mark base; they do not multiply each other.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000002","name":"Perfect Balance — Blacksmithing — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-universal-perfect-balance"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000002","name":"Perfect Balance","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Balance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Weapon grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to one chosen Athletics manoeuvre made using it. Enable the Mark condition only while using this weapon for that manoeuvre. No Bulk reduction.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000003","name":"Reinforced Edge — Blacksmithing — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-universal-reinforced-edge"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000003","name":"Reinforced Edge","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reinforced Edge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Weapon deals +3 damage per weapon damage die against objects. At Core Tier 5+, this becomes +5 per die. Enable the object-target toggle; this does not ignore Hardness. Sundering Drive — Two actions, once per encounter: make one Strike with this weapon against an object. On a hit, add 3 × Core Tier damage before Hardness. This Strike counts toward multiple attack penalty normally; the additional damage is resolved manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000004","name":"Fortified Frame — Blacksmithing — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-universal-fortified-frame"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000004","name":"Fortified Frame","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Fortified Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Armor or shield has ×2 pre-Mark maximum item HP at Core Tiers 1–3, ×3 at Tiers 4–5, and ×4 at Tier 6, plus 2 × Core Tier Hardness. Other durability bonuses add against the same pre-Mark base, not this multiplied value. This does not grant wearer HP or AC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000005","name":"Master Reforge — Blacksmithing — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-universal-master-reforge"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000005","name":"Master Reforge","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Master Reforge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Rebuilding recovers 90% of recorded ordinary components, rounded down, and preserves compatible Marks. Recovered value cannot exceed actual inputs; no duplicated items or components. Unique resources require GM approval.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000006","name":"Ember Temper — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-1-ember-temper"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000006","name":"Ember Temper","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Ember Temper</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Weapon sheds controllable light and deals additional fire damage equal to 4 × Core Tier on a critical hit only.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000007","name":"Blood Temper — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-1-blood-temper"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000007","name":"Blood Temper","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Blood Temper</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>While the wielder is at or below half maximum HP, this weapon deals +4 × Core Tier damage. This is the wielder&#39;s HP, not the target&#39;s.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000008","name":"Hellfire Channel — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-1-hellfire-channel"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000008","name":"Hellfire Channel","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Hellfire Channel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Once per encounter, ignite the weapon for 1 minute. Its Strikes deal additional Core Tier d8 fire damage. Fire resistance is reduced by 3 × Core Tier against this added damage only, minimum 0; immunity is unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000009","name":"Tormentor's Edge — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-1-tormentors-edge"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000009","name":"Tormentor's Edge","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tormentor&#39;s Edge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Once per round after this weapon critically hits, the target attempts a Will save against your higher class or spell DC. Failure: frightened 2; critical failure: frightened 3 and fleeing until the end of its next turn. Success: no effect. This is a mental, fear effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000010","name":"Executioner's Ember — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-1-perfected-killing-edge"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000010","name":"Executioner's Ember","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Executioner&#39;s Ember</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>A weapon deals additional precision damage equal to Core Tier d8 against a creature at or below half maximum HP. Enable the Mark condition only against an eligible target. Precision immunity applies.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000011","name":"Soul-Burned Steel — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-1-soul-burned-steel"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000011","name":"Soul-Burned Steel","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Soul-Burned Steel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Reaction, once per day when damage would reduce you to 0 HP without killing you outright: remain at 1 HP, Step up to 15 feet and make one Strike with this weapon. Afterwards gain drained 1 until daily preparations. It does not prevent death effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000012","name":"Consecrated Finish — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-2-consecrated-finish"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000012","name":"Consecrated Finish","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Consecrated Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>While worn or wielded, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Religion checks to Recall Knowledge about undead or fiends. Enable the Mark condition for an eligible subject. The item bears a visible sacred dedication; it does not automatically bypass sanctification requirements.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000013","name":"Dawnbound — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-2-dawnbound"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000013","name":"Dawnbound","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dawnbound</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Weapon deals +3 spirit damage per weapon damage die against undead and fiends. Other targets gain no added damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000014","name":"Guardian's Radiance — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-2-guardians-radiance"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000014","name":"Guardian's Radiance","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Guardian&#39;s Radiance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Reaction, once per round when an ally within 15 feet takes damage: reduce that instance by 6 × Core Tier, minimum 0. Requires the item worn or wielded; does not redirect damage to you.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000015","name":"Aegis of Dawn — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-2-aegis-of-dawn"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000015","name":"Aegis of Dawn","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Aegis of Dawn</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Worn armor grants +12 × Core Tier maximum HP and spirit and void resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. This is maximum HP, not temporary HP or healing; repeated equipping must not restore damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000016","name":"Martyr's Forge — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-2-martyrs-forge"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000016","name":"Martyr's Forge","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Martyr&#39;s Forge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Reaction, once per encounter when an ally within 30 feet takes damage: take unpreventable damage equal to your level and reduce the ally&#39;s instance by 8 × your level, minimum 0. You cannot use this if the sacrifice would reduce you to 0 HP.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000017","name":"Solar Ascension — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-2-solar-ascension"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000017","name":"Solar Ascension","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Solar Ascension</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Two actions, once per day: for 1 minute radiate bright light in a 30-foot aura. Allies including you gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to AC and saves while inside. Undead and fiends starting their turns inside take 3 × Core Tier d6 spirit damage, basic Will save against your higher class or spell DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000018","name":"Diagnostic Matrix — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-3-diagnostic-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000018","name":"Diagnostic Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Diagnostic Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>While wielded or worn, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Crafting checks to Repair or Identify Magic involving this item&#39;s mechanism. Enable the Mark condition only when this item is the subject; its display also reports damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000019","name":"Integrated Conduit — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-3-integrated-conduit"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000019","name":"Integrated Conduit","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Integrated Conduit</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>The item can accommodate two additional Mana or Aetherglass component sockets without added Bulk. Supply their materials normally. Sockets do not grant free Marks, Capacity, or Core progression.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000020","name":"Adaptive Configuration — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-3-adaptive-configuration"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000020","name":"Adaptive Configuration","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adaptive Configuration</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Choose three legal weapon damage types or tool configurations at creation. One Interact action switches the active mode. Only one mode applies at a time; it cannot grant extra Marks or combine incompatible weapon statistics.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000021","name":"Arcane Mechanism — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-3-arcane-mechanism"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000021","name":"Arcane Mechanism","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Mechanism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Two actions, once per encounter: emit a 30-foot line dealing 2 × Core Tier d8 electricity damage with a basic Reflex save against your higher class or spell DC. Mechanism must be wielded. This is an electricity and magical effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000022","name":"Phase Mechanism — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-3-phase-mechanism"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000022","name":"Phase Mechanism","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Phase Mechanism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>One action, once per encounter: Stride up to your Speed through creatures and up to 10 feet of non-magical solid obstacles. End in an open space you can perceive; if none is reachable, the action fails without moving. This is magical movement, not teleportation.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000023","name":"Reality Engine — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"blacksmithing-specialty-3-reality-engine"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000023","name":"Reality Engine","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reality Engine</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>One action, once per day: for 1 minute, once on each of your turns reduce one two-action activation of this item&#39;s other Marks to one action. Cannot reduce spellcasting, reactions, free actions, or this activation; does not refresh uses or bypass prerequisites.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000024","name":"Stable Formula — Alchemy — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-universal-stable-formula"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000024","name":"Stable Formula","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stable Formula</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>A dose lasts four times its normal shelf life and resists mundane temperature spoilage while sealed. This does not extend its effect duration or preserve an opened dose indefinitely.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000025","name":"Efficient Batch — Alchemy — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-universal-efficient-batch"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000025","name":"Efficient Batch","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Efficient Batch</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>A batch produces 25% additional identical doses, rounded down, minimum one extra per four paid doses. Bonus doses are outputs, not additional inputs for applying this Mark again.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000026","name":"Refined Reagent — Alchemy — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-universal-refined-reagent"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000026","name":"Refined Reagent","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Refined Reagent</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Choose one fixed healing, movement-distance or resistance value at creation; multiply that value by 2 when the dose is used. Do not multiply DCs, damage, action counts, condition values, or resource returns.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000027","name":"Quick Preparation — Alchemy — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-universal-quick-preparation"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000027","name":"Quick Preparation","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Quick Preparation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Reduce this batch&#39;s required artisan-days by 40%, rounded up to whole days with a minimum of one. Apply to the original duration, not repeatedly to previously reduced work.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000028","name":"Catalyst Reserve — Alchemy — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-universal-catalyst-reserve"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000028","name":"Catalyst Reserve","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Catalyst Reserve</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Reduce one named secondary ordinary resource cost by 25%, rounded down, minimum one unit still required. It cannot reduce Core, unique ingredients or its own catalyst cost.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000029","name":"Measured Dose — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-1-measured-dose"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000029","name":"Measured Dose","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Measured Dose</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>Halve one fixed numerical drawback of this dose, rounding its magnitude down. Cannot remove addiction, death, ability loss, action costs or a drawback that defines the item&#39;s identity.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000030","name":"Concentrated — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-1-concentrated"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000030","name":"Concentrated","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Concentrated</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>Multiply this dose&#39;s HP healing by 3. If it grants temporary HP instead, add only 10 temporary HP to a separately tracked Artisan buffer; never multiply the original temporary HP. The buffer expires with the dose and cannot be refreshed by re-equipping.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000031","name":"Extended Formula — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-1-extended-formula"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000031","name":"Extended Formula","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Extended Formula</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>An effect lasting at least 1 minute lasts four times as long, maximum 24 hours. Does not extend persistent damage, poison stages, resource regeneration or another Mark&#39;s effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000032","name":"Rapid Infusion — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-1-rapid-infusion"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000032","name":"Rapid Infusion","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Rapid Infusion</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>One action: draw this accessible dose and consume or administer it to a willing adjacent creature. No extra Interact action is required. A dose is still consumed; this does not make an unwilling target willing.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000033","name":"Restorative Panacea — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-1-restorative-panacea"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000033","name":"Restorative Panacea","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Restorative Panacea</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>On consumption, restore 8 × Core Tier additional HP and reduce two of clumsy, enfeebled, frightened, sickened or stupefied by 2, minimum 0. Attempt one counteract check against poison or disease using the drinker&#39;s higher class/spell DC minus 10 and counteract rank equal to Core Tier. Ongoing sources can reapply conditions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000034","name":"Phoenix Draught — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-1-phoenix-draught"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000034","name":"Phoenix Draught","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Phoenix Draught</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>One action to drink. Once per day per creature, for 1 hour: the first damage that would reduce you to 0 HP without outright death instead leaves you at 1 HP and restores 10 × Core Tier HP. The draught then ends. It cannot prevent death effects or be chained with another Phoenix Draught.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000035","name":"Masked Toxin — Alchemy — Venomcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-2-masked-toxin"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000035","name":"Masked Toxin","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Masked Toxin</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>The DC to detect this poison before exposure increases by Core Tier + 2. Its saving throw DC is unchanged; an identified poison remains identified.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000036","name":"Adhesive Poison — Alchemy — Venomcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-2-adhesive-poison"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000036","name":"Adhesive Poison","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adhesive Poison</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>An applied injury poison survives misses and affects the next two successful weapon hits before the end of the encounter. Each hit follows normal exposure rules; hitting one creature twice does not create two independent copies of the same affliction.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000037","name":"Swift Venom — Alchemy — Venomcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-2-swift-venom"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000037","name":"Swift Venom","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Swift Venom</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>The poison&#39;s onset is immediate. On an initial failed save apply stage 1 immediately; on a critical failure apply stage 2 if available. Subsequent intervals are unchanged. A poison already having immediate onset gains +Core Tier to its initial save DC only.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000038","name":"Predator Formula — Alchemy — Venomcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-2-predator-formula"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000038","name":"Predator Formula","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predator Formula</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Choose one creature trait such as dragon, fiend or undead at creation. The poison gains +Core Tier + 2 to its save DC against that trait. This does not bypass poison immunity.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000039","name":"Mutagenic Venom — Alchemy — Venomcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-2-mutagenic-venom"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000039","name":"Mutagenic Venom","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mutagenic Venom</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Choose clumsy, enfeebled or stupefied at creation. When the poison reaches stage 3, apply the chosen condition at 3 for 1 round. The rider triggers at most once per round per creature and does not permanently change its stage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000040","name":"Perfect Killer — Alchemy — Venomcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-2-perfect-killer"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000040","name":"Perfect Killer","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Killer</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Poison save DC increases by 5. Once per target per dose, treat the first ordinary success as a failure; critical successes are unchanged. Poison immunity still applies, and the dose cannot retrigger this benefit via transfer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000041","name":"Purified Matrix — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-3-purified-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000041","name":"Purified Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Purified Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Remove up to three mundane impurities from a component without losing material quantity. Cannot remove curses, change rarity or erase an intrinsic hazardous magical property.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000042","name":"Alchemical Alloy — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-3-alchemical-alloy"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000042","name":"Alchemical Alloy","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Alchemical Alloy</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Combine two paid same-tier material families into one component with both native tags. Choose one family for numerical Core progression; never add both Core progressions together.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000043","name":"Composite Matrix — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-3-composite-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000043","name":"Composite Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Composite Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>One composite component can satisfy two compatible family requirements. Pay both quantities and use the lower tier for eligibility; the benefit is sharing one socket, not free materials.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000044","name":"Refined Substance — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-3-refined-substance"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000044","name":"Refined Substance","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Refined Substance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>For one named Mark&#39;s Anchor eligibility only, treat this component as two tiers higher, maximum 6. Its actual tier, Core progression, sale value and other Marks are unchanged.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000045","name":"Philosopher's Matrix — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-3-philosophers-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000045","name":"Philosopher's Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Philosopher&#39;s Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Once per project replace up to two missing ordinary resource families with equal quantities of paid same-tier resources. Cannot substitute unique, dragon-origin or story-gated ingredients.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000046","name":"Living Transmutation — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"alchemy-specialty-3-living-transmutation"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000046","name":"Living Transmutation","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Transmutation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Create three paid, compatible material identities for this component. Choose one during daily preparations. Native tags and eligibility change, but existing Marks must remain legal and only one identity supplies Core statistics.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000047","name":"Stable Matrix — Enchanting — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-universal-stable-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000047","name":"Stable Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stable Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>The item gains +Core Tier + 2 to its DC against counteract attempts targeting its magic. This protects the item only, not the bearer&#39;s spells, and does not make it immune to suppression. Spellbreak Guard — Two actions, once per encounter: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to your next saving throw against a spell before the start of your next turn. Wield or wear the item throughout. This does not counteract the spell and must be applied manually to that save.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000048","name":"Attuned Craft — Enchanting — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-universal-attuned-craft"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000048","name":"Attuned Craft","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Attuned Craft</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>During daily preparations authorise up to six named bearers to use this item&#39;s custom activations. An unauthorised user cannot activate them; it remains usable as an ordinary item. No effect on native spellcasting or ownership.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000049","name":"Resonant Channel — Enchanting — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-universal-resonant-channel"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000049","name":"Resonant Channel","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Channel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>Add two charges to one explicitly identified custom daily charge pool on this item. These charges return only at daily preparations; they cannot fuel charge-regeneration or Mark-refresh effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000050","name":"Efficient Activation — Enchanting — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-universal-efficient-activation"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000050","name":"Efficient Activation","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Efficient Activation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>Free action, once per encounter immediately before using this item&#39;s two-action custom activation: reduce it to one action. Cannot affect spellcasting, change use limits or combine with another action reduction on the same activation.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000051","name":"Arcane Safeguard — Enchanting — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-universal-arcane-safeguard"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000051","name":"Arcane Safeguard","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Safeguard</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>Reduce self-damage from this item&#39;s own overload or critical activation failure by 75%, rounding damage down. Other creatures and normal enemy attacks are unaffected. Non-damage drawbacks remain.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000052","name":"Minor Empowerment — Enchanting — Aethercasting","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-1-minor-empowerment"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000052","name":"Minor Empowerment","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Minor Empowerment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Gain an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to one chosen narrow skill use. Enable the Mark condition only for the agreed use, not all checks with that skill.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000053","name":"Focused Empowerment — Enchanting — Aethercasting","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-1-focused-empowerment"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000053","name":"Focused Empowerment","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Focused Empowerment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Gain an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to one selected skill or initiative while this item is wielded or worn.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000054","name":"Twin Empowerment — Enchanting — Aethercasting","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-1-twin-empowerment"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000054","name":"Twin Empowerment","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Twin Empowerment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Choose two different skills at creation. While wielded or worn gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to checks with both. Record the choices on the item; neither can be an attack, AC or spell DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000055","name":"Overcharged Matrix — Enchanting — Aethercasting","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-1-overcharged-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000055","name":"Overcharged Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Overcharged Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Free action, once per encounter before one roll: add 5 to one existing positive flat Artisan bonus on this item for that roll only. Cannot improve Over-Potency, a multiplier, DC, condition, resource quantity or another Overcharged Matrix. This cannot raise the +2 per-Mark Over-Potency cap.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000056","name":"Overlord Matrix — Enchanting — Aethercasting","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-1-overlord-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000056","name":"Overlord Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Overlord Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>While wielded or held, weapon gains +2 Artisan Bonus to its attack rolls, or spell focus gains +2 Artisan Bonus to spell attack and spell DC. This Over-Potency is capped at +2 per Mark beyond Core progression and stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000057","name":"Aetherheart Lattice — Enchanting — Aethercasting","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-1-aetherheart-lattice"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000057","name":"Aetherheart Lattice","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Aetherheart Lattice</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>One action, three charges per day: refresh one expended once-per-encounter Standard or Major activation on this item. Each target activation can be refreshed once per day. Cannot refresh charges, healing, recovery, action-reduction or other refresh effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000058","name":"Minor Binding — Enchanting — Essencebinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-2-minor-binding"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000058","name":"Minor Binding","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Minor Binding</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>At creation add two descriptive utility tags from the component&#39;s source, such as luminous or water-resistant. They unlock compatible crafting requirements but grant no numerical Core progression or creature immunities.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000059","name":"Bound Trait — Enchanting — Essencebinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-2-bound-trait"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000059","name":"Bound Trait","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Bound Trait</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Weapon gains two chosen compatible traits from trip, shove, disarm or versatile B/P/S. Record the exact traits at creation. This does not add reach, deadly or fatal.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000060","name":"Elemental Essence — Enchanting — Essencebinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-2-elemental-essence"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000060","name":"Elemental Essence","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Elemental Essence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Weapon deals additional Core Tier d8 damage of a selected acid, cold, electricity or fire type. Worn armor or held shield instead grants resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier to that type. Resistance uses the highest source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000061","name":"Predatory Essence — Enchanting — Essencebinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-2-predatory-essence"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000061","name":"Predatory Essence","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predatory Essence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Choose at creation either precise darkvision 60 feet, imprecise scent 30 feet, climb Speed 30 feet or swim Speed 30 feet from the harvested essence. Active while worn or wielded; the choice is fixed until recrafted.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000062","name":"Greater Binding — Enchanting — Essencebinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-2-greater-binding"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000062","name":"Greater Binding","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Greater Binding</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Weapon gains +5 feet reach and +2 additional base weapon damage dice. These extra dice use the weapon&#39;s die size and damage type; reach does not improve ranged attacks. Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000063","name":"Living Essence — Enchanting — Essencebinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-2-living-essence"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000063","name":"Living Essence","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Essence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: gain fly Speed equal to land Speed and resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier to the essence&#39;s one chosen energy type. Choose one type at creation from acid, cold, electricity or fire; no immunity is granted.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000064","name":"Runic Signature — Enchanting — Runecarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-3-runic-signature"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000064","name":"Runic Signature","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Runic Signature</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>While worn or held, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Arcana checks involving this artisan&#39;s sigils. Enable the Mark condition only for those sigils.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000065","name":"Resonant Pair — Enchanting — Runecarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-3-resonant-pair"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000065","name":"Resonant Pair","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Pair</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Link two paid items at creation. While both are worn or wielded within 30 feet, each bearer gains +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to saves against the last creature damaged by the other bearer this round. Track the eligible creature manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000066","name":"Layered Inscription — Enchanting — Runecarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-3-layered-inscription"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000066","name":"Layered Inscription","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Layered Inscription</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Choose one Standard Mark on this item and record three legal configurations of its existing choices. Switch one configuration during daily preparations; this does not grant all three benefits or bypass prerequisites.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000067","name":"Runic Feedback — Enchanting — Runecarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-3-runic-feedback"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000067","name":"Runic Feedback","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Runic Feedback</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Reaction, once per round when a linked weapon within 30 feet critically hits: its paired bearer gains +5 Artisan Bonus to their next attack or save before the end of their next turn. A bearer cannot trigger this from their own attack.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000068","name":"Living Rune — Enchanting — Runecarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-3-living-rune"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000068","name":"Living Rune","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Rune</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>One action, once per round: switch one Major-or-lower Mark between two recorded, equally costed configurations. Used charges and frequency limits remain spent across configurations; switching cannot refresh effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000069","name":"Grand Glyph — Enchanting — Runecarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"enchanting-specialty-3-grand-glyph"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000069","name":"Grand Glyph","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Glyph</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Three actions, once per day: place a visible 20-foot-radius glyph within 60 feet for 1 minute. Allies in it gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to AC. Enemies starting turns inside take Core Tier d8 force damage, basic Reflex save against your higher class or spell DC. The glyph is stationary.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000070","name":"Flexible Construction — Leatherwork — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-universal-flexible-construction"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000070","name":"Flexible Construction","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Flexible Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Reduce this armor&#39;s land Speed penalty by 10 feet, minimum 0. It does not grant bonus Speed if the penalty is already absent.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000071","name":"Supple Gussets — Leatherwork — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-universal-perfect-fit"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000071","name":"Supple Gussets","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Supple Gussets</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Acrobatics checks to Squeeze. Physical passage size restrictions still apply.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000072","name":"Tanner's Acid Ward — Leatherwork — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-universal-reinforced-hide"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000072","name":"Tanner's Acid Ward","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tanner&#39;s Acid Ward</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants acid resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. Resistance uses the highest applicable source, not their sum.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000073","name":"Weather Seal — Leatherwork — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-universal-weather-seal"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000073","name":"Weather Seal","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Weather Seal</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Fortitude saves against environmental heat, cold or exposure. Enable the Mark condition only for exposure, not energy attacks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000074","name":"Adaptive Strapping — Leatherwork — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-universal-adaptive-strapping"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000074","name":"Adaptive Strapping","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adaptive Strapping</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Once per round, draw or stow one strapped light item as part of an Interact action using that item. Also secure up to three such items against accidental loss; deliberate Disarm and theft are unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000075","name":"Wyrm Inscription — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-1-wyrm-inscription"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000075","name":"Wyrm Inscription","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Wyrm Inscription</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>The dragon&#39;s identity is visible on the item. While wielded or worn, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Arcana checks about that dragon type. Enable the Mark condition only for that subject.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000076","name":"Draconic Resistance — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-1-draconic-resistance"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000076","name":"Draconic Resistance","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Draconic Resistance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Add 3 × Dragon Tier to this item&#39;s native dragon resistance. This increases one resistance source, not all of the wearer&#39;s resistances.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000077","name":"Scale Dominion — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-1-scale-dominion"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000077","name":"Scale Dominion","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Scale Dominion</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Armor or shield gains +5 × Dragon Tier Hardness and +30 × Dragon Tier item HP. A weapon instead ignores 3 × Dragon Tier resistance against its associated dragon damage type; immunity remains.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Armor, Shield, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000078","name":"Draconic Constitution — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-1-draconic-constitution"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000078","name":"Draconic Constitution","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Draconic Constitution</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Worn armor grants +16 × Dragon Tier maximum HP and +5 Artisan Bonus to saves against its associated damage type; green scales apply to poison. Maximum HP is not healing.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000079","name":"Wyrm's Fury — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-1-wyrms-fury"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000079","name":"Wyrm's Fury","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Wyrm&#39;s Fury</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Weapon gains +3 additional base weapon damage dice, using its existing die size and damage type. This Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000080","name":"Dragonheart Awakening — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-1-dragonheart-awakening"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000080","name":"Dragonheart Awakening","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dragonheart Awakening</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: gain fly Speed equal to twice land Speed and increase this item&#39;s native dragon resistance by 5 × Dragon Tier. Once during the duration, use two actions for a 30-foot cone dealing 3 × Dragon Tier d8 of the scale&#39;s damage type, basic Reflex against your higher class or spell DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000081","name":"Trophy Memory — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-2-trophy-memory"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000081","name":"Trophy Memory","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Trophy Memory</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>While worn or wielded, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Nature checks to Recall Knowledge about the source creature family. Enable the Mark condition only for that family.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000082","name":"Predator's Sense — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-2-predators-sense"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000082","name":"Predator's Sense","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predator&#39;s Sense</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>While worn, gain imprecise scent 30 feet and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Survival checks to Track the source creature family. Scent detects presence, not precise location; record the source family on the item.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000083","name":"Natural Movement — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-2-natural-movement"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000083","name":"Natural Movement","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Natural Movement</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Choose a source-appropriate climb or swim Speed at creation. Worn armor grants that Speed at 40 feet and +10 feet to land Speed in one recorded natural terrain. Terrain does not change during combat.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000084","name":"Apex Hide — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-2-apex-hide"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000084","name":"Apex Hide","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Apex Hide</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Worn armor grants +10 × Core Tier maximum HP and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Fortitude saves against one recorded creature theme: poison, cold or disease. This replaces the former start-of-combat temporary HP grant.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000085","name":"Apex Trait — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-2-apex-trait"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000085","name":"Apex Trait","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Apex Trait</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Worn armor grants imprecise tremorsense 30 feet while you share a solid surface with the target, and doubles your ordinary Leap distance. Tremorsense does not detect airborne creatures or bypass concealment.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000086","name":"Chimera Binding — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-2-chimera-binding"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000086","name":"Chimera Binding","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Chimera Binding</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Free action once per round: select one of two recorded creature-source senses or movement modes for this item. Once per day, both can be active for 10 minutes. Pay for both source components; no access to unrecorded creature abilities.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000087","name":"Trophy Finish — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-3-trophy-finish"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000087","name":"Trophy Finish","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Trophy Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Intimidation checks when the visible trophy is relevant to the audience. Enable the Mark condition only then; it is not mental control.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000088","name":"Whiteout Mantle — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-3-weather-mantle"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000088","name":"Whiteout Mantle","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Whiteout Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants cold resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier and an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to Survival. It does not grant weather immunity.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000089","name":"Predator's Cloak — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-3-predators-cloak"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000089","name":"Predator's Cloak","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predator&#39;s Cloak</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth and Survival in one recorded terrain. Free action once per round after successfully Hiding there: Step up to 10 feet. The terrain must match the trophy&#39;s source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000090","name":"Court Mantle — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-3-court-mantle"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000090","name":"Court Mantle","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Court Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Diplomacy and Society in formal settings. Allies within 15 feet who can see you gain +3 Artisan Bonus to saves against fear while you are conscious; adjudicate the aura manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000091","name":"Dread Sovereign Pelt — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-3-sovereign-pelt"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000091","name":"Dread Sovereign Pelt","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dread Sovereign Pelt</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Intimidation and Survival. A predator&#39;s presence dominates the hunt and the negotiation table without removing social consequences.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000092","name":"Legendary Pelt — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"leatherwork-specialty-3-legendary-pelt"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000092","name":"Legendary Pelt","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Legendary Pelt</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>One action, once per day for 1 minute: become invisible. After each hostile action the invisibility is suppressed until the start of your next turn. While invisible this way, gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth; invisibility is not undetectability.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000093","name":"Seasoned Construction — Carpentry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-universal-seasoned-construction"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000093","name":"Seasoned Construction","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Seasoned Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>Wooden armor or shield resists mundane warping and gains +100% of pre-Mark maximum item HP. This additive durability bonus does not multiply other Mark bonuses.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000094","name":"Light Frame — Carpentry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-universal-light-frame"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000094","name":"Light Frame","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Light Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>Reduce Bulk by 2, minimum 0, when the wooden frame forms most of this item. Contents and attached equipment retain their own Bulk.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000095","name":"Precision Joinery — Carpentry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-universal-precision-joinery"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000095","name":"Precision Joinery","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Precision Joinery</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>While held or worn, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Crafting checks to Repair this item or operate its mechanism. Enable the Mark condition only for that mechanism.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000096","name":"Skyhunter Limbs — Carpentry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-universal-reinforced-limb"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000096","name":"Skyhunter Limbs","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Skyhunter Limbs</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>A ranged weapon deals +3 × Core Tier damage against flying or falling targets. Enable the Mark condition only against an airborne target.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000097","name":"Modular Frame — Carpentry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-universal-modular-frame"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000097","name":"Modular Frame","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Modular Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>During daily preparations replace up to three ordinary wooden components with paid compatible alternatives. Retain legal Marks and maker records; no free resources, Capacity or extra active Core progression.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000098","name":"True Fletching — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-true-fletching"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000098","name":"True Fletching","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>True Fletching</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to attacks affected by ordinary wind. Enable the Mark condition only during such wind. Magical wind and range penalties remain.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000099","name":"Specialist Ammo Chamber — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-specialist-ammo-chamber"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000099","name":"Specialist Ammo Chamber","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Specialist Ammo Chamber</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Ranged weapon accepts two recorded compatible specialist ammunition families. Ammunition is paid and consumed normally; this does not enable ammunition of the wrong weapon category.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000100","name":"Longshot Construction — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-longshot-construction"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000100","name":"Longshot Construction","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Longshot Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Double this ranged weapon&#39;s range increment. Normal increment penalties and line of effect still apply; this does not increase melee reach.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000101","name":"Rapid Mechanism — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-rapid-mechanism"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000101","name":"Rapid Mechanism","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Rapid Mechanism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Free action once per round: reload this ranged weapon by up to two Interact actions. Supply ammunition and a free hand normally. A reload-0 weapon instead gains +5 Artisan Bonus to its next Strike this turn; these options are exclusive.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000102","name":"Horizonstring — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-perfected-tension"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000102","name":"Horizonstring","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Horizonstring</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>A ranged weapon grants +2 Artisan Bonus to attacks against targets beyond its first range increment. This Over-Potency bonus is capped at +2 per Mark. Enable the Mark condition only at that distance. Normal range penalties still apply.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000103","name":"Warbow Overdraw — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-warbow-overdraw"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000103","name":"Warbow Overdraw","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Warbow Overdraw</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +3 additional base weapon damage dice using its own die size and type. After a natural 1 on a Strike, you are off-guard until the start of your next turn. Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000104","name":"Builder's Mark — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-builders-mark"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000104","name":"Builder's Mark","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Builder&#39;s Mark</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Inspecting this wooden construction grants +Core Tier + 2 to Crafting checks to identify weaknesses or plan repairs. The mark records load paths; no actor effect is created.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000105","name":"Reinforced Frame — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-reinforced-frame"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000105","name":"Reinforced Frame","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reinforced Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Wooden structure or vehicle gains ×3 pre-Mark maximum HP and +4 × Core Tier Hardness. Other durability bonuses add from the same base rather than compounding.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000106","name":"Rapid Assembly — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-rapid-assembly"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000106","name":"Rapid Assembly","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Rapid Assembly</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Qualifying construction or field fortification takes half its original artisan-days, minimum one. Apply once to original work, not recursively after other reductions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000107","name":"Modular Construction — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-modular-construction"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000107","name":"Modular Construction","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Modular Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Recover 90% of recorded ordinary inputs when dismantling, rounded down; unique inputs require GM adjudication. Re-deploy the stored modules in one-quarter normal assembly time, minimum 10 minutes.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000108","name":"Grand Design — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-grand-design"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000108","name":"Grand Design","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Design</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Choose recurring Lumber or repair cost: reduce it by 40%, minimum one unit. Gain +5 on the structure&#39;s principal construction check. These are campaign project benefits, not character Crafting bonuses.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000109","name":"Citadel Framework — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-citadel-framework"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000109","name":"Citadel Framework","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Citadel Framework</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Defenders gain +5 to checks and saves against forced entry, collapse and siege movement while within the fortification. Gates and walls gain structural damage resistance equal to 8 × Core Tier.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000110","name":"Carved Grip — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-carved-grip"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000110","name":"Carved Grip","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Carved Grip</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 to your DC against Disarm attempts targeting this weapon. It does not protect other held items or prevent voluntary dropping.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000111","name":"Wolf Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-wolf-carving"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000111","name":"Wolf Carving","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Wolf Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Free action once per round after this weapon hits: Stride up to half Speed toward that target. Movement must end closer and triggers reactions normally.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000112","name":"Bear Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-bear-carving"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000112","name":"Bear Carving","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Bear Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>While the shield is raised, gain physical resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier; against damage caused by forced movement, use 6 × Core Tier instead. Use only the applicable value, not both.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000113","name":"Serpent Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-serpent-carving"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000113","name":"Serpent Carving","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Serpent Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Weapon gains +5 feet melee reach. Free action once per round after hitting: Step up to 15 feet; this movement does not trigger that target&#39;s reactions. Other creatures react normally if applicable.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000114","name":"Spirit Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-spirit-carving"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000114","name":"Spirit Carving","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Spirit Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>One action, once per encounter for 1 minute: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to this weapon&#39;s attacks and imprecise scent 30 feet. This is a magical spirit manifestation; it grants no extra actions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000115","name":"Totemic Ascendance — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-totemic-ascendance"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000115","name":"Totemic Ascendance","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Totemic Ascendance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Athletics, +20 feet land Speed and resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier to physical damage. A visible animal spirit surrounds the wearer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000116","name":"Stonebound — Stonemasonry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-universal-stonebound"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000116","name":"Stonebound","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stonebound</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>Armor or shield gains +50% of its pre-Mark maximum item HP and +2 × Core Tier Hardness. The stone protects the item, not its wearer&#39;s HP. Durability bonuses add against the same pre-Mark base.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000117","name":"Perfect Foundation — Stonemasonry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-universal-perfect-foundation"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000117","name":"Perfect Foundation","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Foundation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on checks to stabilise or repair a structure built on this foundation. Its reference lines reveal subsidence before ordinary collapse.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000118","name":"Anchored Construction — Stonemasonry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-universal-anchored-construction"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000118","name":"Anchored Construction","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Anchored Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>Structure gains +Core Tier + 2 to its DC against forced movement or toppling and counts as two sizes larger for those contests. It can still be damaged or destroyed.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000119","name":"Load-Bearing Cut — Stonemasonry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-universal-load-bearing-cut"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000119","name":"Load-Bearing Cut","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Load-Bearing Cut</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>Stone structure gains +100% of pre-Mark maximum HP. This adds to other durability bonuses using the same base; it does not grant character HP.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000120","name":"Resonant Stone — Stonemasonry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-universal-resonant-stone"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000120","name":"Resonant Stone","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Stone</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>The component can provide both ward and arcane-anchor tags for compatible work. Tags grant eligibility only, not extra Capacity, Core progression or free Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000121","name":"Mason's Seal — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-masons-seal"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000121","name":"Mason's Seal","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mason&#39;s Seal</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on Crafting checks to identify damage, load paths or reconstruction methods in the sealed stonework. Inspection reveals non-magical hidden cavities within 5 feet of the examined surface.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000122","name":"Enduring Monument — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-enduring-monument"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000122","name":"Enduring Monument","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Enduring Monument</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Monument has ×4 pre-Mark maximum HP and +5 × Core Tier Hardness. Durability bonuses add from the pre-Mark base rather than multiplying one another.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000123","name":"Grand Foundation — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-grand-foundation"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000123","name":"Grand Foundation","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Foundation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Structures on this foundation gain +5 against collapse, subsidence and siege movement. Repairs restore twice normal item HP without consuming additional ordinary repair materials.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000124","name":"Civic Wonder — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-civic-wonder"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000124","name":"Civic Wonder","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Civic Wonder</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Choose Culture, Defence, Trade, Faith or Infrastructure at creation. Once per Kingdom turn gain +5 on one project check directly serving that purpose. The wonder also acts as a recognised landmark; no automatic income is created.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000125","name":"Imperial Work — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-imperial-work"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000125","name":"Imperial Work","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Imperial Work</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Reduce one named recurring Kingdom resource cost tied to this structure by 40%, minimum one unit. Once per Kingdom turn reroll one failed maintenance check for it and use the new result.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000126","name":"World-Rooted Foundation — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-world-rooted-foundation"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000126","name":"World-Rooted Foundation","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>World-Rooted Foundation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>The structure cannot be moved or toppled by non-magical effects. It gains structural damage resistance equal to 12 × Core Tier; magical displacement requires a counteract check against the completed project&#39;s recorded DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000127","name":"Inscribed Keystone — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-2-inscribed-keystone"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000127","name":"Inscribed Keystone","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Inscribed Keystone</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on checks to identify or repair this ward. Authorised users can read its owner, purpose and whether it has been breached.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000128","name":"Sentinel Rune — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-2-sentinel-rune"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000128","name":"Sentinel Rune","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sentinel Rune</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>Detect a recorded creature trait crossing the site&#39;s boundary within 300 feet of the rune. Alert up to six designated creatures anywhere inside the site; this is an alarm, not precise tracking or a hostile effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000129","name":"Sanctuary Ward — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-2-sanctuary-ward"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000129","name":"Sanctuary Ward","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sanctuary Ward</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>A stationary 30-foot zone grants authorised allies +5 to saves while inside. Once per creature per day on entering, restore 10 × Core Tier HP. Leaving and re-entering does not refresh healing.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000130","name":"War Rune — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-2-war-rune"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000130","name":"War Rune","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>War Rune</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>In a stationary 30-foot zone, authorised defenders gain +5 to attack rolls and +3 × Core Tier damage on their first successful Strike each round. The rune does not move with a bearer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000131","name":"Fortress Sigil — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-2-fortress-sigil"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000131","name":"Fortress Sigil","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Fortress Sigil</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>Hostile teleportation or planar entry into the recorded site requires a counteract check against the project&#39;s recorded DC +5. Failure prevents entry and spends the attempt normally; authorised travel is unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000132","name":"Dominion Ward — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-2-dominion-ward"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000132","name":"Dominion Ward","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dominion Ward</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>One recorded hostile creature trait suffers -5 to attacks and saves within a 60-foot ward. Those creatures cannot use ordinary concealment against authorised defenders; invisibility and total cover remain unless separately overcome.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000133","name":"Titanic Fit — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-3-titanic-fit"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000133","name":"Titanic Fit","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Titanic Fit</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Ignore up to 3 Bulk belonging to this stone item while properly worn or wielded, minimum 0. Contents and other equipment are unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000134","name":"Anchored — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-3-anchored"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000134","name":"Anchored","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Anchored</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>While worn or raised, gain +5 to the DC against Trip or Reposition and count as two sizes larger for resisting forced movement. This does not increase your actual size or offensive manoeuvre limits.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000135","name":"Earthshaker — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-3-earthshaker"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000135","name":"Earthshaker","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Earthshaker</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Free action once per round after a critical weapon hit or successful Shield Block: choose an adjacent enemy. Fortitude against your higher class/spell DC: failure pushes it 10 feet and makes it off-guard until the end of its next turn; critical failure also knocks it prone. No effect on success.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000136","name":"Basalt Bastion — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-3-mountain-plate"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000136","name":"Basalt Bastion","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Basalt Bastion</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier and an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to Fortitude saves.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000137","name":"Heart of the Mountain — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-3-mountain-blood-plate"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000137","name":"Heart of the Mountain","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Heart of the Mountain</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier, an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Fortitude saves, and -5 feet to land Speed. Physical resistances use the highest source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000138","name":"Living Colossus — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-3-living-colossus"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000138","name":"Living Colossus","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Colossus</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: grow one size category, gain +10 feet melee reach, +5 Artisan Bonus to Athletics and physical resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier. End in sufficient space; equipment enlarges but its sale value and permanent Bulk do not change.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000139","name":"Perfect Clarity — Glassmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-universal-perfect-clarity"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000139","name":"Perfect Clarity","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Clarity</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>A held optic grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Perception checks involving visual detail. Enable the Mark condition only when viewing through the optic; it does not bypass concealment. Stored Flare — Three actions (Concentrate, Manipulate, Light), once per day: release stored light in a 15-foot emanation. Creatures other than you attempt a Fortitude save against your higher class or spell DC: failure dazzled for Core Tier rounds; critical failure blinded for 1 round, then dazzled for Core Tier rounds; success unaffected. Resolve saves and conditions manually. This is a visual effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000140","name":"Glarecut Glass — Glassmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-universal-hardened-glass"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000140","name":"Glarecut Glass","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Glarecut Glass</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>A held focus grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to visual Seek checks. Enable the Mark condition when sight applies; concealment is not negated.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000141","name":"Arcane Lens — Glassmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-universal-arcane-lens"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000141","name":"Arcane Lens","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Lens</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>The optical component grants arcane, optic and conductor tags and can provide two compatible lens sockets. Supply their materials and Marks normally; no Capacity increase.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000142","name":"Precision Focus — Glassmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-universal-precision-focus"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000142","name":"Precision Focus","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Precision Focus</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to attacks against a target you successfully Sought this turn using the mounted optic. Enable the Mark condition only for that target and turn. Prismatic Sightline — Two actions, once per encounter: Seek using the optic, then make one ranged Strike with this weapon against a creature you detected. Ignore ordinary concealment for that Strike, but not hidden, undetected or total cover. Normal multiple attack penalty applies.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000143","name":"Shatter Safe — Glassmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-universal-shatter-safe"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000143","name":"Shatter Safe","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shatter Safe</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>Twice per day when damage would destroy this glass-bearing item, it instead remains at 1 item HP. This protects the item only; worn-item protection does not prevent bearer damage. Record spent uses manually. Shatter Ward — Reaction. Trigger: damage would destroy this item. Spend one of this Mark&#39;s two daily uses to leave it at 1 item HP instead. This is the activation cost of its existing protection, not additional uses; it never prevents damage to the bearer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000144","name":"Surveyor's Reticle — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-1-calibrated-lens"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000144","name":"Surveyor's Reticle","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Surveyor&#39;s Reticle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>A held focus grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to initiative. Read the battlefield before the first blow.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000145","name":"Focusing Lens — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-1-focusing-lens"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000145","name":"Focusing Lens","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Focusing Lens</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>Increase the ranged weapon&#39;s range increment by 50%. The mounted optical sight does not affect melee reach or remove range penalties.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000146","name":"Spectrum Prism — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-1-spectrum-prism"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000146","name":"Spectrum Prism","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Spectrum Prism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>Choose two energy types from acid, cold, electricity or fire at creation. Free action once per round before this weapon&#39;s Strike: convert all its added energy damage from the first type to the second, or back. Base physical damage is unchanged.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000147","name":"Beam Splitter — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-1-beam-splitter"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000147","name":"Beam Splitter","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Beam Splitter</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>Reaction, once per encounter after a ranged weapon Strike hits: make a second Strike against a different target within 30 feet of the first, using the same multiple attack penalty as the triggering Strike. This additional Strike counts toward later attacks; pay ammunition normally.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000148","name":"Trueglass Crown — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-1-trueglass-crown"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000148","name":"Trueglass Crown","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Trueglass Crown</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>Worn armor reveals invisible creatures to you within 60 feet as concealed rather than invisible. Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves against visual illusions. It does not see through walls or automatically disbelieve illusions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000149","name":"Sovereign Refraction — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-1-crown-prism"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000149","name":"Sovereign Refraction","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sovereign Refraction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>A held spell focus grants +2 Artisan Bonus to spell DC and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Arcana, with a -1 Artisan spell-attack penalty. The Over-Potency spell DC bonus is capped at +2 per Mark. Requires a Tier 5+ optical Anchor. Its power favours save spells.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000150","name":"Perfect Reflection — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-2-perfect-reflection"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000150","name":"Perfect Reflection","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Reflection</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>A held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Deception checks to Impersonate using the mirror to prepare your disguise. Enable the Mark condition only for that prepared disguise.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000151","name":"Truth Mirror — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-2-truth-mirror"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000151","name":"Truth Mirror","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Truth Mirror</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>A held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Perception checks to Sense Motive or detect a visual disguise through the mirror. Enable the Mark condition only for those checks; no automatic lie detection. Unmask — One action, once per encounter: attempt to counteract one visual illusion affecting a creature or object seen through the mirror within 30 feet. Use your higher class or spell DC minus 10 for the counteract modifier and Core Tier as counteract rank. Ordinary disguises instead permit one immediate Seek check.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000152","name":"Reflective Ward — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-2-reflective-ward"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000152","name":"Reflective Ward","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reflective Ward</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>Reaction, once per encounter when a spell attack targets you: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to AC against that attack. If it critically misses, deal Core Tier d8 force damage to its caster within 60 feet, basic Reflex against your higher class/spell DC. This is retaliation, not a copied spell.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000153","name":"Doppelglass — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-2-doppelglass"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000153","name":"Doppelglass","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Doppelglass</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>One action, once per encounter: gain concealed until the start of your next turn. The first attack that misses because of this flat check lets you Step 10 feet as a free action; this movement does not end the concealment.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000154","name":"Gate Mirror — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-2-gate-mirror"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000154","name":"Gate Mirror","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Gate Mirror</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>Three actions, once per day: open a two-way portal between this mirror and its paid, attuned partner within 10 miles on the same plane for 1 minute. Up to six willing creatures may cross. Both exits require open space; dimensional wards can block passage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000155","name":"Mirror Lord — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-2-mirror-lord"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000155","name":"Mirror Lord","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mirror Lord</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: once per round use your reaction when targeted by a spell attack to counteract it using your higher class/spell DC minus 10 and counteract rank equal to Core Tier. Success negates it; critical success also deals 2 × Core Tier d8 force damage to the caster, basic Reflex against that DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000156","name":"Stable Cell — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-3-stable-cell"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000156","name":"Stable Cell","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stable Cell</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Recorded magical charges cannot decay from ordinary time or environmental exposure. Once per day ignore one effect that would drain a single charge; this does not stop deliberate use or regenerate spent charges.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000157","name":"Mana Reservoir — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-3-mana-reservoir"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000157","name":"Mana Reservoir","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mana Reservoir</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Add three daily charges to one named custom activation on this item. Charges cannot fuel recovery, extra-charge or refresh effects and return only at daily preparations. Reservoir Lance — Two actions, once per encounter: expend one charge from the named pool to deal 2 × Core Tier d6 force damage to one creature within 60 feet, basic Reflex against your higher class or spell DC. This does not restore or create charges; resolve damage and charge spending manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000158","name":"Arcane Conductor — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-3-arcane-conductor"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000158","name":"Arcane Conductor","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Conductor</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Weapon gains +2 additional base weapon damage dice from a luminous glass channel. Use its existing die size and type; this Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000159","name":"Overflow Channel — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-3-overflow-channel"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000159","name":"Overflow Channel","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Overflow Channel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Free action once per encounter before a damaging item activation: add Core Tier d8 damage of that activation&#39;s primary damage type. If it costs charges, pay one additional charge. Applies once to one damage roll, not persistent or repeated damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000160","name":"Crystal Matrix — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-3-crystal-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000160","name":"Crystal Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Crystal Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Reduce the Capacity cost of one compatible paid Enchanting or Azlanti Artifice Mark by 2, minimum 1. Does not grant a free Mark or raise maximum Capacity. Multiple discounts apply to the original cost, never below 1.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000161","name":"Eternity Cell — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"glassmaking-specialty-3-eternity-cell"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000161","name":"Eternity Cell","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Eternity Cell</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Add five charges per day to one named custom activation. Once per encounter when you critically succeed at an attack or save, recover one charge spent on that activation. Cannot fuel charge generation, resource recovery, healing or refresh effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000162","name":"Emberproof Glaze — Pottery — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-universal-hardened-ceramic"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000162","name":"Emberproof Glaze","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Emberproof Glaze</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>Worn armor or a held shield grants fire resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. Resistance uses the highest applicable source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000163","name":"Thermal Craft — Pottery — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-universal-thermal-craft"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000163","name":"Thermal Craft","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Thermal Craft</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>Contents remain at their stored mundane temperature for 24 hours while sealed. The vessel ignores ordinary heat/cold damage from storage; attacks, spells and bearer damage are unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000164","name":"Sealed Vessel — Pottery — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-universal-sealed-vessel"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000164","name":"Sealed Vessel","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sealed Vessel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>Contents cannot leak, evaporate or become mundanely contaminated until the vessel is destroyed, not merely Broken. Does not preserve a consumed dose or increase storage capacity.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000165","name":"Shock-Fired — Pottery — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-universal-shock-fired"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000165","name":"Shock-Fired","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shock-Fired</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>The ceramic item gains +Core Tier + 2 to its DC or checks against shattering and rupture effects. This is item protection, not a bonus to the bearer&#39;s saves.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000166","name":"Nested Chamber — Pottery — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-universal-nested-chamber"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000166","name":"Nested Chamber","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Nested Chamber</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>Add three concealed internal chambers, each holding one light dose or object. Their contents count toward Bulk; searching the chambers uses the normal concealment rules with +Core Tier + 2 to the item&#39;s concealment DC. Chamber Draw — One action (Manipulate): retrieve one object from a chamber into a free hand. This does not activate, drink or use the retrieved object; those actions retain their normal costs.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000167","name":"Fired Seal — Pottery — Ceramancy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-1-fired-seal"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000167","name":"Fired Seal","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Fired Seal</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>While worn or held, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Crafting checks to Repair or identify this ceramic item. Enable the Mark condition only when working on this item.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000168","name":"Ceramic Plate — Pottery — Ceramancy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-1-ceramic-plate"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000168","name":"Ceramic Plate","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Ceramic Plate</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>Armor or shield gains +5 × Core Tier Hardness and +40 × Core Tier item HP without increased Bulk. This improves the item, not wearer maximum HP. Kiln Renewal — Two actions, once per encounter: touch the armor or shield to restore 8 × Core Tier item HP, up to its maximum. It must not be destroyed. This repairs the item, never its wearer&#39;s HP.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000169","name":"Living Clay — Pottery — Ceramancy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-1-living-clay"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000169","name":"Living Clay","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Clay</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>At the start of the wearer&#39;s turn during an encounter, repair this item for 5 × Core Tier HP if it is not destroyed. Outside encounters it repairs once per minute. It cannot restore missing components or the wearer&#39;s HP.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000170","name":"Terracotta Guardian — Pottery — Ceramancy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-1-terracotta-guardian"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000170","name":"Terracotta Guardian","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Terracotta Guardian</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>Three actions, once per day: animate a guardian for 1 minute using a creature stat block recorded at creation, maximum level equal to twice Core Tier. It has the minion trait and requires one action to command; no independent extra turns or summoning abilities. The GM approves the exact stat block.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000171","name":"Adaptive Ceramic — Pottery — Ceramancy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-1-adaptive-ceramic"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000171","name":"Adaptive Ceramic","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adaptive Ceramic</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>Reaction once per round before taking bludgeoning, piercing or slashing damage: gain resistance equal to 6 × Core Tier against that type, including the triggering damage, until the start of your next turn. Other physical types are unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000172","name":"Living Ceramic Shell — Pottery — Ceramancy","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-1-living-ceramic-shell"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000172","name":"Living Ceramic Shell","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Ceramic Shell</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>Worn armor grants +20 × Core Tier maximum HP. At the start of each encounter turn repair the armor itself for 4 × Core Tier item HP. Replaces regenerating temporary HP; removing or re-equipping grants no healing.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000173","name":"Sanctified Vessel — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-2-sanctified-vessel"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000173","name":"Sanctified Vessel","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sanctified Vessel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>While holding the vessel, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Religion checks to identify its contained essence. Enable the Mark condition for that essence only. Mundane spiritual leakage is prevented.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000174","name":"Essence Vessel — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-2-essence-vessel"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000174","name":"Essence Vessel","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Essence Vessel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>Store up to three separately sealed harvested essences without ordinary degradation. They remain distinct paid inputs; opening one chamber does not consume or expose the others.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000175","name":"Bound Spirit — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-2-bound-spirit"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000175","name":"Bound Spirit","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Bound Spirit</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>Record a willing spirit and one Lore at creation. While holding the vessel gain +5 Artisan Bonus to checks with that Lore; the spirit can speak to its bearer. It grants neither extra turns nor access to undisclosed creature abilities.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000176","name":"Sealed Curse — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-2-sealed-curse"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000176","name":"Sealed Curse","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sealed Curse</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>A successfully contained curse cannot spread while this vessel remains intact. Gain +5 on attempts to counteract the contained curse using the normal counteract procedure. The containment itself requires resolving the curse, not simply placing this Mark.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000177","name":"Release Matrix — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-2-release-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000177","name":"Release Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Release Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>Two actions, once per day: discharge one paid stored essence in a 30-foot cone for 3 × Core Tier d8 spirit damage, basic Will against your higher class/spell DC. Consume the essence; recharging requires another compatible harvested essence.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000178","name":"Grand Reliquary — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-2-grand-reliquary"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000178","name":"Grand Reliquary","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Reliquary</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>Hold three paid compatible essences. Two actions once per day: consume two to heal up to six willing creatures within 30 feet for 8 × Core Tier HP each and reduce their frightened by 2. Refilling does not reset the daily use.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000179","name":"Heatproof Glaze — Pottery — Pyroceramics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-3-heatproof-glaze"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000179","name":"Heatproof Glaze","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Heatproof Glaze</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>The vessel ignores ordinary forge heat and gains +Core Tier + 2 to checks against magical thermal breakage. This does not protect the bearer from fire damage or create a resistance aura.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000180","name":"Thermal Crucible — Pottery — Pyroceramics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-3-thermal-crucible"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000180","name":"Thermal Crucible","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Thermal Crucible</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>When processing heat-sensitive ordinary materials, recover 30% of otherwise lost units, rounded down. Recovery cannot exceed recorded loss and cannot be recycled through the same process for new material.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000181","name":"Fragmenting Casing — Pottery — Pyroceramics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-3-fragmenting-casing"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000181","name":"Fragmenting Casing","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Fragmenting Casing</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>A bomb gains 10 feet additional splash radius and +3 × Core Tier splash damage. Allies in the enlarged area are affected normally; do not multiply direct-hit damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000182","name":"Shaped Charge — Pottery — Pyroceramics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-3-shaped-charge"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000182","name":"Shaped Charge","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shaped Charge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>On use choose concentrated detonation: remove all splash damage and add Core Tier d12 primary damage against the directly hit creature or object. A miss does not deal this additional damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000183","name":"Pressure Vessel — Pottery — Pyroceramics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-3-pressure-vessel"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000183","name":"Pressure Vessel","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Pressure Vessel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>Multiply the explosive&#39;s base primary damage dice by 3. Do not multiply flat bonuses, splash, persistent damage or added Mark dice. A critical manufacturing failure destroys the paid ordinary casing inputs.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000184","name":"Furnace Heart — Pottery — Pyroceramics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"pottery-specialty-3-furnace-heart"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000184","name":"Furnace Heart","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Furnace Heart</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>Two actions, once per day: a 20-foot emanation deals 3 × Core Tier d8 fire damage to other creatures, basic Reflex against your higher class/spell DC. The item also serves as a portable forge for downtime when set down safely.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000185","name":"Lightweave — Weaving — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-universal-lightweave"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000185","name":"Lightweave","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Lightweave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>Reduce this primarily textile item&#39;s Bulk by 2, minimum 0. This does not reduce the Bulk of its contents or other carried equipment.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000186","name":"Perfect Thread — Weaving — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-universal-perfect-thread"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000186","name":"Perfect Thread","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Thread</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on the next Tailoring or Leatherwork project check that consumes this textile. Once consumed, the thread cannot grant this benefit to a second project.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000187","name":"Slipknot Weave — Weaving — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-universal-reinforced-weave"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000187","name":"Slipknot Weave","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Slipknot Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Athletics and Acrobatics checks to Escape, not unarmed Escape attacks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000188","name":"Weatherproof Weave — Weaving — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-universal-weatherproof-weave"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000188","name":"Weatherproof Weave","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Weatherproof Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>Worn armor ignores ordinary rain exposure and grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Fortitude saves against severe non-magical weather. Enable the Mark condition only for weather.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000189","name":"Tensioned Thread — Weaving — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-universal-tensioned-thread"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000189","name":"Tensioned Thread","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tensioned Thread</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>A woven weapon gains +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Athletics checks to Grapple or Trip with it. Enable the Mark condition only when using that weapon, and it must already have the relevant trait.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000190","name":"Resonant Thread — Weaving — Aetherweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-1-resonant-thread"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000190","name":"Resonant Thread","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Thread</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Textile supplies mana, conductor and aetherwoven tags for compatible work. Its visible pattern grants +Core Tier + 2 to identify its own magic; it does not add free Marks or spell slots.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000191","name":"Manaweave — Weaving — Aetherweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-1-manaweave"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000191","name":"Manaweave","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Manaweave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier to one chosen acid, cold, electricity or fire type. Use the highest applicable resistance source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000192","name":"Spellthread — Weaving — Aetherweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-1-spellthread"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000192","name":"Spellthread","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Spellthread</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Two actions once per day: restore 6 × Core Tier HP to one willing touched creature and let it immediately Step up to 10 feet. This is a magical restoration activation, not a stored spell slot.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000193","name":"Ethereal Weave — Weaving — Aetherweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-1-ethereal-weave"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000193","name":"Ethereal Weave","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Ethereal Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Ignore non-magical ground difficult terrain while wearing this armor. Free action once per encounter: Step up to 20 feet through occupied creature spaces, ending in an open space. Does not pass through walls.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000194","name":"Expanded Matrix — Weaving — Aetherweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-1-expanded-matrix"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000194","name":"Expanded Matrix","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Expanded Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Reduce the Capacity cost of one compatible paid Enchanting or Tailoring Mark by 2, minimum 1. Total costs still cannot exceed Core Capacity. Discounts apply to the original cost, not recursively.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000195","name":"Aetherbound Form — Weaving — Aetherweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-1-aetherbound-form"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000195","name":"Aetherbound Form","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Aetherbound Form</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Two actions once per day for 1 minute: gain fly Speed 40 feet, physical resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier, and squeeze through openings as though two sizes smaller. You are not incorporeal and cannot pass through solid walls.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000196","name":"Warcloth Finish — Weaving — Ironweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-2-warcloth-finish"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000196","name":"Warcloth Finish","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Warcloth Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Textile armor gains +100% of pre-Mark maximum item HP. This does not increase wearer HP; other durability bonuses use the same original base.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000197","name":"Impact Mesh — Weaving — Ironweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-2-impact-mesh"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000197","name":"Impact Mesh","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Impact Mesh</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. Resistance does not add to other physical-resistance sources. Impact Lock — Two actions, once per encounter: until the start of your next turn, increase this Mark&#39;s physical resistance to 6 × Core Tier. This replaces its passive resistance for that duration; do not add the two together. Resolve the temporary increase manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000198","name":"Flexible Weave — Weaving — Ironweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-2-flexible-weave"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000198","name":"Flexible Weave","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Flexible Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Reduce this armor&#39;s land Speed penalty by 15 feet, minimum 0, and raise its Dexterity modifier cap by 3. This changes the armor cap, not your Dexterity score.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000199","name":"Shock-Absorbing Warcloth — Weaving — Ironweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-2-shock-absorbing-warcloth"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000199","name":"Shock-Absorbing Warcloth","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shock-Absorbing Warcloth</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants +12 × Core Tier maximum HP. This replaces per-turn temporary HP; it does not heal when equipped or grant damage absorption beyond the maximum-HP increase.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000200","name":"Silken Steel — Weaving — Ironweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-2-silken-steel"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000200","name":"Silken Steel","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Silken Steel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants +5 Artisan Bonus to AC beyond Core progression and physical resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier. AC stacks with different Marks; resistance uses the highest source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000201","name":"Lifeline Braid — Weaving — Ironweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-2-unbreakable-braid"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000201","name":"Lifeline Braid","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Lifeline Braid</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants bleed resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier and an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Athletics and Acrobatics checks to Escape, not unarmed Escape attacks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000202","name":"Heraldic Seal — Weaving — Heraldweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-3-heraldic-seal"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000202","name":"Heraldic Seal","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Heraldic Seal</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society checks proving the authority or affiliation displayed by this worn armor. Enable the Mark condition only where that affiliation matters.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000203","name":"Unbroken Standard — Weaving — Heraldweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-3-unbroken-standard"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000203","name":"Unbroken Standard","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Unbroken Standard</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>While this focus is held and displayed, allies within 30 feet who can see it gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to saves against fear. The bearer must be conscious; resolve recipients manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000204","name":"Marching Banner — Weaving — Heraldweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-3-marching-banner"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000204","name":"Marching Banner","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Marching Banner</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Allies starting their turns within 30 feet of the displayed focus gain +15 feet Artisan land Speed for that turn and ignore the first 15 feet of difficult terrain. Does not grant extra actions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000205","name":"King's Colours — Weaving — Heraldweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-3-kings-colours"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000205","name":"King's Colours","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>King&#39;s Colours</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Allies within 30 feet of the displayed focus gain +5 Artisan Bonus to Aid checks and saves against mental effects while they can see its conscious bearer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000206","name":"Conqueror's Standard — Weaving — Heraldweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-3-conquerors-standard"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000206","name":"Conqueror's Standard","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Conqueror&#39;s Standard</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Two actions once per encounter for 1 minute: when an ally within 30 feet reduces a hostile creature to 0 HP, that ally gains +5 Artisan Bonus to attacks until the end of its next turn. Multiple defeats refresh duration, not bonus magnitude.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000207","name":"Sovereign Standard — Weaving — Heraldweaving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"weaving-specialty-3-sovereign-standard"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000207","name":"Sovereign Standard","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sovereign Standard</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Two actions once per day for 1 minute: allies within 30 feet gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves and +3 × Core Tier damage on their first hit each round. On activation grant each ally a separately tracked 10-point Artisan temporary-HP buffer, expiring after 1 minute. Do not overwrite class temporary HP; record and deduct the buffer manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000208","name":"Perfect Index — Bookmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-universal-perfect-index"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000208","name":"Perfect Index","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Index</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>Find any recorded entry in this held focus immediately. Gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society checks to Recall Knowledge directly documented in it; enable the Mark condition only for that subject.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000209","name":"Preserved Knowledge — Bookmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-universal-preserved-knowledge"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000209","name":"Preserved Knowledge","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Preserved Knowledge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>The work is immune to mundane water, ageing and mildew. A legible copy of damaged pages can be restored during one hour of study if at least half the original survives; it does not recover erased magical secrets.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000210","name":"Master Copy — Bookmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-universal-master-copy"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000210","name":"Master Copy","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Master Copy</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>Copy a paid formula or mundane text in one-quarter normal downtime, minimum 10 minutes. Material and licence costs remain; copying does not duplicate magic, consumables or activation charges.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000211","name":"Encoded Script — Bookmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-universal-encoded-script"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000211","name":"Encoded Script","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Encoded Script</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 to the DC to Decipher Writing in this focus without its key. Authorised readers can read normally; possession of a stolen key bypasses the encoding.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000212","name":"Reference Tabs — Bookmaking — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-universal-reference-tabs"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000212","name":"Reference Tabs","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reference Tabs</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>Free action once per 10 minutes before Recall Knowledge using this held focus&#39;s recorded subject: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to that check. No benefit on an undocumented subject.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000213","name":"Indexed Arcana — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-1-indexed-arcana"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000213","name":"Indexed Arcana","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Indexed Arcana</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Arcana checks about spells recorded in it. Enable the Mark condition only for those spells; the index locates their entries immediately.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000214","name":"Mnemonic Pages — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-1-mnemonic-pages"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000214","name":"Mnemonic Pages","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mnemonic Pages</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Once per day after 10 minutes of study, replace up to three unexpended prepared spells with known spells of the same ranks. Does not restore spent slots or grant spells the reader cannot normally prepare.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000215","name":"Resonant Chapter — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-1-resonant-chapter"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000215","name":"Resonant Chapter","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Chapter</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Choose one spell trait at creation. Spells with that trait gain +3 damage per spell rank on their first damage roll against each target. This is flat bonus damage, not multiplied ongoing damage; record the chosen trait.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000216","name":"Spell Echo — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-1-spell-echo"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000216","name":"Spell Echo","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Spell Echo</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Reaction once per encounter after a spell deals damage to one target: deal additional damage equal to Core Tier d8 of its primary type to that target or a second creature within 15 feet. Basic Reflex against your spell DC. This is a separate magical echo and cannot echo itself.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000217","name":"Archmage Codex — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-1-archmage-codex"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000217","name":"Archmage Codex","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Archmage Codex</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Elemental Thesis — Choose Acid, Cold, Electricity, Fire or Sonic when applying this Mark. While holding this spell focus, damaging spells bearing the chosen elemental trait gain bonus damage of that type. Passive formula: 2 × spell damage die (3 × at Core Tier 6). Ascendant Thesis — Two actions, once per encounter for 1 minute: replace the passive bonus with (Core Tier + 2) × spell damage die. Use the chosen type&#39;s first base damage component and its largest die; if that type is absent, use the spell&#39;s first base component. Flat-only components provide no bonus dice. Example: Core Tier 4 with a d6 spell adds 2d6 passively or 6d6 while activated. Add this once to initial damage, not each missile, persistent tick or later repeated damage. Enable Initial Spell Damage only for that roll. Enable Ascendant Thesis after activation and clear it when the minute ends. Uses and duration are tracked manually; active and passive dice never add together.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000218","name":"Endless Grimoire — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-1-endless-grimoire"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000218","name":"Endless Grimoire","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Endless Grimoire</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Three actions once per day: recover one expended spell slot of rank no higher than Core Tier, maximum 6. It cannot recover a slot used to create permanent resources, restore slots or activate another recovery effect. Non-slot casters require a recorded equivalent before crafting.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000219","name":"Scholar's Index — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-2-scholars-index"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000219","name":"Scholar's Index","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Scholar&#39;s Index</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>Held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society research checks on its documented subject. Enable the Mark condition only during that research.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000220","name":"Lore Codex — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-2-lore-codex"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000220","name":"Lore Codex","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Lore Codex</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>After 10 minutes study choose one recorded narrow Lore. Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to checks with that Lore for 8 hours, even if untrained, but do not gain proficiency ranks or trained-only actions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000221","name":"Crafting Manual — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-2-crafting-manual"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000221","name":"Crafting Manual","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Crafting Manual</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>For one recorded recipe family reduce required artisan-days by 40%, minimum one, and gain +5 to its first project check each day. Reductions use original work; this does not create free materials.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000222","name":"Tactical Treatise — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-2-tactical-treatise"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000222","name":"Tactical Treatise","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tactical Treatise</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>Free action once per encounter before an attack, save or Recall Knowledge against a documented creature trait: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to that roll. The trait is chosen at creation and must match the target.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000223","name":"Master's Testament — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-2-masters-testament"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000223","name":"Master's Testament","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Master&#39;s Testament</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>During daily preparations choose one of three recorded skill feats whose level and other prerequisites you meet. Gain its use until next preparations. No ancestry, class, dedication or spellcasting feats; it cannot grant crafting outputs retroactively.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000224","name":"Legendary Chronicle — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-2-legendary-chronicle"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000224","name":"Legendary Chronicle","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Legendary Chronicle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>Up to six readers study for 10 minutes during daily preparations. Each gains +5 Artisan Bonus to one recorded narrow Lore for the day and one fortune reroll of a failed check with that Lore, using the new result. Restudying does not reset uses.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000225","name":"Surveyor's Mark — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-3-surveyors-mark"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000225","name":"Surveyor's Mark","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Surveyor&#39;s Mark</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>Held map grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Survival checks to navigate its recorded territory. Enable the Mark condition only within mapped territory.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000226","name":"Safe Passage — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-3-safe-passage"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000226","name":"Safe Passage","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Safe Passage</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>In mapped territory reduce travel delays from documented non-magical hazards by 50%. Does not increase encounter Speed, remove hazards outright or reduce an undelayed journey.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000227","name":"Resource Survey — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-3-resource-survey"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000227","name":"Resource Survey","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resource Survey</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>A successful survey reveals one hidden ordinary resource site and grants +5 on the first extraction check there each Kingdom turn. No resource is created without a site; unique discoveries remain GM-controlled.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000228","name":"Strategic Map — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-3-strategic-map"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000228","name":"Strategic Map","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Strategic Map</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>Held map grants +5 Artisan Bonus to initiative in its recorded region when studied for 10 minutes earlier that day. Enable the Mark condition only within the studied region.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000229","name":"Hidden Paths — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-3-hidden-paths"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000229","name":"Hidden Paths","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Hidden Paths</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>Establish a mapped secret route: travel along it takes half normal non-combat time and travellers gain +5 to avoid detection on the route. It cannot cross impassable terrain or ignore hostile fortifications.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000230","name":"World Atlas — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"bookmaking-specialty-3-world-atlas"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000230","name":"World Atlas","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>World Atlas</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>At each Kingdom turn choose one mapped region: double ordinary resource output, halve ordinary travel time, or gain +5 on settlement-planning checks there for that turn. Only one mode applies; never duplicate unique or story resources.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000231","name":"Tailored First Impression — Tailoring — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-universal-perfect-fit"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000231","name":"Tailored First Impression","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tailored First Impression</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Diplomacy checks to Make an Impression. This does not compel agreement or bypass attitudes.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000232","name":"Steadfast Hem — Tailoring — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-universal-reinforced-seam"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000232","name":"Steadfast Hem","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Steadfast Hem</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to Will saves against fear. Enable the Mark condition only against fear effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000233","name":"Hidden Pocketing — Tailoring — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-universal-hidden-pocketing"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000233","name":"Hidden Pocketing","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Hidden Pocketing</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Thievery checks to Conceal an Object in its fitted pockets. Enable the Mark condition only for an object that fits; Bulk is unchanged.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000234","name":"Quick-Access Cut — Tailoring — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-universal-quick-access-cut"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000234","name":"Quick-Access Cut","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Quick-Access Cut</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Once per round draw one accessible light object as part of the action that uses it. Also secure two additional light objects against accidental loss. Does not reduce the use action&#39;s cost.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000235","name":"Layered Lining — Tailoring — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-universal-layered-lining"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000235","name":"Layered Lining","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Layered Lining</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Garment supports two paid secondary textile or leather components without additional empty-lining Bulk. Materials and Marks still cost normally; this grants no Capacity or duplicate Core progression.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000236","name":"Combat Cut — Tailoring — Battlestitching","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-1-combat-cut"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000236","name":"Combat Cut","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Combat Cut</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Acrobatics checks to Tumble Through. It does not change movement cost or negate reactions from a failed check.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000237","name":"Quickdraw Harness — Tailoring — Battlestitching","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-1-quickdraw-harness"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000237","name":"Quickdraw Harness","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Quickdraw Harness</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Free action once per round: draw up to two weapons secured to this harness, provided you have enough free hands. It does not make a Strike or reduce other activation costs.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000238","name":"Vital Reinforcement — Tailoring — Battlestitching","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-1-vital-reinforcement"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000238","name":"Vital Reinforcement","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Vital Reinforcement</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Worn armor grants +18 × Core Tier maximum HP. This is maximum HP, not temporary HP or healing; repeated equipping must not restore damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000239","name":"Reactive Weave — Tailoring — Battlestitching","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-1-reactive-weave"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000239","name":"Reactive Weave","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reactive Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Reaction once per round when damaged: reduce that damage instance by 6 × Core Tier, or 10 × Core Tier if caused by a critical hit, minimum 0. This is reduction of one instance, not resistance for the round.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000240","name":"Duelist's War-Skin — Tailoring — Battlestitching","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-1-war-skin"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000240","name":"Duelist's War-Skin","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Duelist&#39;s War-Skin</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Worn armor grants Artisan Bonuses of Core Tier to AC and Reflex saves, and 5 × Core Tier feet to land Speed. It grants no physical resistance.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000241","name":"War-Skin Regeneration — Tailoring — Battlestitching","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-1-war-skin-regeneration"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000241","name":"War-Skin Regeneration","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>War-Skin Regeneration</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Worn armor grants +24 × Core Tier maximum HP. Once per day after an encounter, spend 10 minutes adjusting it to restore 8 × Core Tier HP. Replaces per-turn temporary HP and cannot heal through repeated equipping.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000242","name":"Silent Stitch — Tailoring — Veilcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-2-silent-stitch"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000242","name":"Silent Stitch","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Silent Stitch</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Stealth checks where clothing noise matters. Enable the Mark condition only when muffling the garment would help.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000243","name":"Chameleon Cloth — Tailoring — Veilcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-2-chameleon-cloth"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000243","name":"Chameleon Cloth","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Chameleon Cloth</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth checks to Hide or Sneak in one recorded environment palette. Enable the Mark condition only there; no half-Speed requirement beyond normal Sneak rules.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000244","name":"Many-Faced Weave — Tailoring — Veilcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-2-many-faced-weave"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000244","name":"Many-Faced Weave","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Many-Faced Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>One minute of adjustment creates a recorded mundane disguise of clothing and facial framing. Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to Deception checks to Impersonate that identity. No size change or copied abilities; close examination still permits detection.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000245","name":"Shadow Mantle — Tailoring — Veilcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-2-shadow-mantle"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000245","name":"Shadow Mantle","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shadow Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>One action once per encounter for 1 minute: gain concealed in dim light or darkness and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth there. Attacking does not end concealment, but bright light suppresses it until you leave that light.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000246","name":"Phase Veil — Tailoring — Veilcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-2-phase-veil"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000246","name":"Phase Veil","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Phase Veil</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>One action once per encounter until the end of your next turn: move through creature spaces and non-magical difficult terrain, gaining physical resistance equal to 6 × Core Tier. You cannot cross solid walls and must end movement in open space.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000247","name":"Null Mantle — Tailoring — Veilcraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-2-null-mantle"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000247","name":"Null Mantle","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Null Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>One action once per day for 1 minute: become invisible and gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves against magical detection. Hostile actions suppress invisibility until the start of your next turn. Does not negate precise non-visual senses.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000248","name":"Court Finish — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-3-court-finish"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000248","name":"Court Finish","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Court Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society checks involving formal protocol or heraldry. Enable the Mark condition only for those subjects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000249","name":"Envoy's Raiment — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-3-envoys-raiment"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000249","name":"Envoy's Raiment","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Envoy&#39;s Raiment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Diplomacy checks when acting in an officially recognised capacity. Enable the Mark condition only with a relevant mandate; social consequences still apply. Envoy&#39;s Reprise — Free action, once per day after failing a Diplomacy check made in your recognised official capacity: reroll and use the new result. This is a fortune effect; it cannot combine with another fortune effect on that roll.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000250","name":"Commander's Mantle — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-3-commanders-mantle"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000250","name":"Commander's Mantle","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Commander&#39;s Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Conscious wearer visibly leading allies grants those allies within 30 feet +5 Artisan Bonus to Aid checks and saves against fear. The wearer is not their own ally for this aura; record recipients manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000251","name":"Judicator's Robes — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-3-judicators-robes"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000251","name":"Judicator's Robes","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Judicator&#39;s Robes</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to Perception checks to Sense Motive. One action once per encounter: designate a visible creature within 60 feet; allies gain +5 Artisan Bonus to their first save against it before the end of your next turn.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000252","name":"Sovereign Presence — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-3-sovereign-presence"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000252","name":"Sovereign Presence","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sovereign Presence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Two actions once per encounter for 1 minute: allies within 30 feet gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves. Enemies within 30 feet take -3 Artisan Bonus to saves against your fear effects. This is a mental aura; unconsciousness ends it.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000253","name":"Coronation Regalia — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"tailoring-specialty-3-coronation-regalia"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000253","name":"Coronation Regalia","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Coronation Regalia</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Worn armor grants its recognised office-holder +18 × Core Tier maximum HP and +5 Artisan Bonus to Diplomacy and Intimidation. Two actions once per day: allies within 30 feet gain a separately tracked 10-point Artisan temporary-HP buffer for 10 minutes. Do not overwrite class temporary HP; track and deduct this buffer manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmCraftingGuide1","name":"Wrathmaker — Crafting Handbook","ownership":{"default":2},"pages":[{"_id":"wmCraftingRules1","name":"Crafting, gathering and recovery","type":"text","sort":0,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\n<h1>Wrathmaker Crafting</h1>\n<p>The experimental Workbench is enabled by the GM. Open Craft to select a base item, recipe, Core material and Tier. Required materials come from the selected Party Stash.</p>\n<h2>Solo or together</h2><p>Every supported recipe can be crafted by one lead artisan. Material specialists are optional: they unlock their own eligible Marks and combinations rather than permission to make the base item. The usual recipe checks and material requirements still apply.</p>\n<p>Up to six different artisans can work together. Each assigned artisan contributes to the same Work Block and commits the same calendar downtime. Progress is the work-block result multiplied by the number of distinct artisans, capped at six. A successful one-day block yields one Progress solo or six with a full team. Failure and critical success are calculated per artisan first. Existing progress is not changed retroactively.</p>\n<h2>Materials and Marks</h2><p>Tiers 1–6 correspond to levels 1, 4, 8, 12, 16 and 20. Material and recipe choices determine the requirements and DC shown in the Workbench. Marks must match the item, artisan, Anchor and minimum Tier. Capacity is shared across the entire item; only one zero-Capacity Mark is allowed. Specialist materials and Mark labour are included in the plan. Adding a specialist does not automatically grant every synergy: the selected Marks must meet their own rules.</p>\n<h2>Reserve, work, confirm</h2><p>Create Project reserves resources so other projects cannot promise the same stock. Work Blocks advance progress without consuming that stock. At completion, review and confirm consumption and creation of the finished item. Cancelling releases unconsumed reservations. The GM can recover a missing completed output without paying again; this is not available after dismantling.</p>\n<h2>Gather</h2><p>Use the Workbench Gather tab to select a character, environment and resource. Available resources may follow the configured region and Tier. The displayed skill, DC and results govern the attempt. The GM chooses whether rewards go to the Party Stash or gathering character.</p>\n<h2>Disassemble</h2><p>Drop a Wrathmaker-formatted item from a character or Party Stash into Disassemble. Review the return before confirming destruction. Recorded items use the original consumption ledger; unrecorded items use a labelled standard-recipe estimate. Recovery is 90%, rounded down per material, Tier and variant. The source item is removed and returns enter the selected Party Stash. Dismantling is irreversible and cannot be repeated on the same item.</p>\n<h2>Automation and activations</h2><p>Supported numerical effects apply automatically. Read each Mark: conditional, target-specific and GM-approved benefits may still require adjudication. An activation button presents its rules; it does not by itself resolve damage, select targets or spend encounter uses. Action costs that are not stated in the source are not invented.</p>\n<h2>Artisan Mark library</h2><p>All Marks, including structure and consumable references, are included as pages in this handbook. The item picker only offers applicable Marks.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000001","name":"Tempered Construction — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tempered Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Armor or shield gains +50% of its pre-Mark maximum item HP and +Core Tier Hardness. This improves the item, not its wearer&#39;s HP. Durability bonuses add against the same pre-Mark base; they do not multiply each other.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000002","name":"Perfect Balance — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Balance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Weapon grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to one chosen Athletics manoeuvre made using it. Enable the Mark condition only while using this weapon for that manoeuvre. No Bulk reduction.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000003","name":"Reinforced Edge — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reinforced Edge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Weapon deals +3 damage per weapon damage die against objects. At Core Tier 5+, this becomes +5 per die. Enable the object-target toggle; this does not ignore Hardness. Sundering Drive — Two actions, once per encounter: make one Strike with this weapon against an object. On a hit, add 3 × Core Tier damage before Hardness. This Strike counts toward multiple attack penalty normally; the additional damage is resolved manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000004","name":"Fortified Frame — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Fortified Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Armor or shield has ×2 pre-Mark maximum item HP at Core Tiers 1–3, ×3 at Tiers 4–5, and ×4 at Tier 6, plus 2 × Core Tier Hardness. Other durability bonuses add against the same pre-Mark base, not this multiplied value. This does not grant wearer HP or AC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000005","name":"Master Reforge — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Master Reforge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Rebuilding recovers 90% of recorded ordinary components, rounded down, and preserves compatible Marks. Recovered value cannot exceed actual inputs; no duplicated items or components. Unique resources require GM approval.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000006","name":"Ember Temper — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Ember Temper</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Weapon sheds controllable light and deals additional fire damage equal to 4 × Core Tier on a critical hit only.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000007","name":"Blood Temper — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Blood Temper</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>While the wielder is at or below half maximum HP, this weapon deals +4 × Core Tier damage. This is the wielder&#39;s HP, not the target&#39;s.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000008","name":"Hellfire Channel — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Hellfire Channel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Once per encounter, ignite the weapon for 1 minute. Its Strikes deal additional Core Tier d8 fire damage. Fire resistance is reduced by 3 × Core Tier against this added damage only, minimum 0; immunity is unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000009","name":"Tormentor's Edge — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tormentor&#39;s Edge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Once per round after this weapon critically hits, the target attempts a Will save against your higher class or spell DC. Failure: frightened 2; critical failure: frightened 3 and fleeing until the end of its next turn. Success: no effect. This is a mental, fear effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000010","name":"Executioner's Ember — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":1000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Executioner&#39;s Ember</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>A weapon deals additional precision damage equal to Core Tier d8 against a creature at or below half maximum HP. Enable the Mark condition only against an eligible target. Precision immunity applies.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000011","name":"Soul-Burned Steel — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":1100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Soul-Burned Steel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Reaction, once per day when damage would reduce you to 0 HP without killing you outright: remain at 1 HP, Step up to 15 feet and make one Strike with this weapon. Afterwards gain drained 1 until daily preparations. It does not prevent death effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000012","name":"Consecrated Finish — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":1200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Consecrated Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>While worn or wielded, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Religion checks to Recall Knowledge about undead or fiends. Enable the Mark condition for an eligible subject. The item bears a visible sacred dedication; it does not automatically bypass sanctification requirements.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000013","name":"Dawnbound — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":1300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dawnbound</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Weapon deals +3 spirit damage per weapon damage die against undead and fiends. Other targets gain no added damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000014","name":"Guardian's Radiance — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":1400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Guardian&#39;s Radiance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Reaction, once per round when an ally within 15 feet takes damage: reduce that instance by 6 × Core Tier, minimum 0. Requires the item worn or wielded; does not redirect damage to you.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000015","name":"Aegis of Dawn — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":1500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Aegis of Dawn</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Worn armor grants +12 × Core Tier maximum HP and spirit and void resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. This is maximum HP, not temporary HP or healing; repeated equipping must not restore damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000016","name":"Martyr's Forge — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":1600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Martyr&#39;s Forge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Reaction, once per encounter when an ally within 30 feet takes damage: take unpreventable damage equal to your level and reduce the ally&#39;s instance by 8 × your level, minimum 0. You cannot use this if the sacrifice would reduce you to 0 HP.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000017","name":"Solar Ascension — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":1700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Solar Ascension</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Two actions, once per day: for 1 minute radiate bright light in a 30-foot aura. Allies including you gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to AC and saves while inside. Undead and fiends starting their turns inside take 3 × Core Tier d6 spirit damage, basic Will save against your higher class or spell DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000018","name":"Diagnostic Matrix — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":1800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Diagnostic Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>While wielded or worn, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Crafting checks to Repair or Identify Magic involving this item&#39;s mechanism. Enable the Mark condition only when this item is the subject; its display also reports damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000019","name":"Integrated Conduit — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":1900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Integrated Conduit</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>The item can accommodate two additional Mana or Aetherglass component sockets without added Bulk. Supply their materials normally. Sockets do not grant free Marks, Capacity, or Core progression.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000020","name":"Adaptive Configuration — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":2000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adaptive Configuration</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Choose three legal weapon damage types or tool configurations at creation. One Interact action switches the active mode. Only one mode applies at a time; it cannot grant extra Marks or combine incompatible weapon statistics.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000021","name":"Arcane Mechanism — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":2100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Mechanism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Two actions, once per encounter: emit a 30-foot line dealing 2 × Core Tier d8 electricity damage with a basic Reflex save against your higher class or spell DC. Mechanism must be wielded. This is an electricity and magical effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000022","name":"Phase Mechanism — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":2200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Phase Mechanism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>One action, once per encounter: Stride up to your Speed through creatures and up to 10 feet of non-magical solid obstacles. End in an open space you can perceive; if none is reachable, the action fails without moving. This is magical movement, not teleportation.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000023","name":"Reality Engine — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":2300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reality Engine</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>One action, once per day: for 1 minute, once on each of your turns reduce one two-action activation of this item&#39;s other Marks to one action. Cannot reduce spellcasting, reactions, free actions, or this activation; does not refresh uses or bypass prerequisites.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000024","name":"Stable Formula — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":2400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stable Formula</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>A dose lasts four times its normal shelf life and resists mundane temperature spoilage while sealed. This does not extend its effect duration or preserve an opened dose indefinitely.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000025","name":"Efficient Batch — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":2500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Efficient Batch</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>A batch produces 25% additional identical doses, rounded down, minimum one extra per four paid doses. Bonus doses are outputs, not additional inputs for applying this Mark again.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000026","name":"Refined Reagent — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":2600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Refined Reagent</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Choose one fixed healing, movement-distance or resistance value at creation; multiply that value by 2 when the dose is used. Do not multiply DCs, damage, action counts, condition values, or resource returns.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000027","name":"Quick Preparation — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":2700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Quick Preparation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Reduce this batch&#39;s required artisan-days by 40%, rounded up to whole days with a minimum of one. Apply to the original duration, not repeatedly to previously reduced work.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000028","name":"Catalyst Reserve — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":2800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Catalyst Reserve</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Reduce one named secondary ordinary resource cost by 25%, rounded down, minimum one unit still required. It cannot reduce Core, unique ingredients or its own catalyst cost.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000029","name":"Measured Dose — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":2900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Measured Dose</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>Halve one fixed numerical drawback of this dose, rounding its magnitude down. Cannot remove addiction, death, ability loss, action costs or a drawback that defines the item&#39;s identity.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000030","name":"Concentrated — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":3000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Concentrated</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>Multiply this dose&#39;s HP healing by 3. If it grants temporary HP instead, add only 10 temporary HP to a separately tracked Artisan buffer; never multiply the original temporary HP. The buffer expires with the dose and cannot be refreshed by re-equipping.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000031","name":"Extended Formula — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":3100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Extended Formula</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>An effect lasting at least 1 minute lasts four times as long, maximum 24 hours. Does not extend persistent damage, poison stages, resource regeneration or another Mark&#39;s effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000032","name":"Rapid Infusion — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":3200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Rapid Infusion</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>One action: draw this accessible dose and consume or administer it to a willing adjacent creature. No extra Interact action is required. A dose is still consumed; this does not make an unwilling target willing.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000033","name":"Restorative Panacea — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":3300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Restorative Panacea</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>On consumption, restore 8 × Core Tier additional HP and reduce two of clumsy, enfeebled, frightened, sickened or stupefied by 2, minimum 0. Attempt one counteract check against poison or disease using the drinker&#39;s higher class/spell DC minus 10 and counteract rank equal to Core Tier. Ongoing sources can reapply conditions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000034","name":"Phoenix Draught — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":3400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Phoenix Draught</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>One action to drink. Once per day per creature, for 1 hour: the first damage that would reduce you to 0 HP without outright death instead leaves you at 1 HP and restores 10 × Core Tier HP. The draught then ends. It cannot prevent death effects or be chained with another Phoenix Draught.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000035","name":"Masked Toxin — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":3500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Masked Toxin</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>The DC to detect this poison before exposure increases by Core Tier + 2. Its saving throw DC is unchanged; an identified poison remains identified.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000036","name":"Adhesive Poison — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":3600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adhesive Poison</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>An applied injury poison survives misses and affects the next two successful weapon hits before the end of the encounter. Each hit follows normal exposure rules; hitting one creature twice does not create two independent copies of the same affliction.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000037","name":"Swift Venom — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":3700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Swift Venom</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>The poison&#39;s onset is immediate. On an initial failed save apply stage 1 immediately; on a critical failure apply stage 2 if available. Subsequent intervals are unchanged. A poison already having immediate onset gains +Core Tier to its initial save DC only.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000038","name":"Predator Formula — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":3800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predator Formula</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Choose one creature trait such as dragon, fiend or undead at creation. The poison gains +Core Tier + 2 to its save DC against that trait. This does not bypass poison immunity.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000039","name":"Mutagenic Venom — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":3900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mutagenic Venom</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Choose clumsy, enfeebled or stupefied at creation. When the poison reaches stage 3, apply the chosen condition at 3 for 1 round. The rider triggers at most once per round per creature and does not permanently change its stage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000040","name":"Perfect Killer — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":4000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Killer</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Poison save DC increases by 5. Once per target per dose, treat the first ordinary success as a failure; critical successes are unchanged. Poison immunity still applies, and the dose cannot retrigger this benefit via transfer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000041","name":"Purified Matrix — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":4100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Purified Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Remove up to three mundane impurities from a component without losing material quantity. Cannot remove curses, change rarity or erase an intrinsic hazardous magical property.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000042","name":"Alchemical Alloy — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":4200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Alchemical Alloy</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Combine two paid same-tier material families into one component with both native tags. Choose one family for numerical Core progression; never add both Core progressions together.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000043","name":"Composite Matrix — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":4300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Composite Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>One composite component can satisfy two compatible family requirements. Pay both quantities and use the lower tier for eligibility; the benefit is sharing one socket, not free materials.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000044","name":"Refined Substance — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":4400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Refined Substance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>For one named Mark&#39;s Anchor eligibility only, treat this component as two tiers higher, maximum 6. Its actual tier, Core progression, sale value and other Marks are unchanged.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000045","name":"Philosopher's Matrix — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":4500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Philosopher&#39;s Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Once per project replace up to two missing ordinary resource families with equal quantities of paid same-tier resources. Cannot substitute unique, dragon-origin or story-gated ingredients.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000046","name":"Living Transmutation — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":4600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Transmutation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Create three paid, compatible material identities for this component. Choose one during daily preparations. Native tags and eligibility change, but existing Marks must remain legal and only one identity supplies Core statistics.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000047","name":"Stable Matrix — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":4700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stable Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>The item gains +Core Tier + 2 to its DC against counteract attempts targeting its magic. This protects the item only, not the bearer&#39;s spells, and does not make it immune to suppression. Spellbreak Guard — Two actions, once per encounter: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to your next saving throw against a spell before the start of your next turn. Wield or wear the item throughout. This does not counteract the spell and must be applied manually to that save.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000048","name":"Attuned Craft — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":4800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Attuned Craft</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>During daily preparations authorise up to six named bearers to use this item&#39;s custom activations. An unauthorised user cannot activate them; it remains usable as an ordinary item. No effect on native spellcasting or ownership.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000049","name":"Resonant Channel — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":4900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Channel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>Add two charges to one explicitly identified custom daily charge pool on this item. These charges return only at daily preparations; they cannot fuel charge-regeneration or Mark-refresh effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000050","name":"Efficient Activation — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":5000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Efficient Activation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>Free action, once per encounter immediately before using this item&#39;s two-action custom activation: reduce it to one action. Cannot affect spellcasting, change use limits or combine with another action reduction on the same activation.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000051","name":"Arcane Safeguard — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":5100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Safeguard</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>Reduce self-damage from this item&#39;s own overload or critical activation failure by 75%, rounding damage down. Other creatures and normal enemy attacks are unaffected. Non-damage drawbacks remain.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000052","name":"Minor Empowerment — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":5200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Minor Empowerment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Gain an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to one chosen narrow skill use. Enable the Mark condition only for the agreed use, not all checks with that skill.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000053","name":"Focused Empowerment — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":5300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Focused Empowerment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Gain an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to one selected skill or initiative while this item is wielded or worn.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000054","name":"Twin Empowerment — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":5400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Twin Empowerment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Choose two different skills at creation. While wielded or worn gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to checks with both. Record the choices on the item; neither can be an attack, AC or spell DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000055","name":"Overcharged Matrix — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":5500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Overcharged Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Free action, once per encounter before one roll: add 5 to one existing positive flat Artisan bonus on this item for that roll only. Cannot improve Over-Potency, a multiplier, DC, condition, resource quantity or another Overcharged Matrix. This cannot raise the +2 per-Mark Over-Potency cap.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000056","name":"Overlord Matrix — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":5600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Overlord Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>While wielded or held, weapon gains +2 Artisan Bonus to its attack rolls, or spell focus gains +2 Artisan Bonus to spell attack and spell DC. This Over-Potency is capped at +2 per Mark beyond Core progression and stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000057","name":"Aetherheart Lattice — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":5700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Aetherheart Lattice</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>One action, three charges per day: refresh one expended once-per-encounter Standard or Major activation on this item. Each target activation can be refreshed once per day. Cannot refresh charges, healing, recovery, action-reduction or other refresh effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000058","name":"Minor Binding — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":5800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Minor Binding</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>At creation add two descriptive utility tags from the component&#39;s source, such as luminous or water-resistant. They unlock compatible crafting requirements but grant no numerical Core progression or creature immunities.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000059","name":"Bound Trait — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":5900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Bound Trait</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Weapon gains two chosen compatible traits from trip, shove, disarm or versatile B/P/S. Record the exact traits at creation. This does not add reach, deadly or fatal.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000060","name":"Elemental Essence — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":6000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Elemental Essence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Weapon deals additional Core Tier d8 damage of a selected acid, cold, electricity or fire type. Worn armor or held shield instead grants resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier to that type. Resistance uses the highest source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000061","name":"Predatory Essence — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":6100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predatory Essence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Choose at creation either precise darkvision 60 feet, imprecise scent 30 feet, climb Speed 30 feet or swim Speed 30 feet from the harvested essence. Active while worn or wielded; the choice is fixed until recrafted.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000062","name":"Greater Binding — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":6200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Greater Binding</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Weapon gains +5 feet reach and +2 additional base weapon damage dice. These extra dice use the weapon&#39;s die size and damage type; reach does not improve ranged attacks. Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000063","name":"Living Essence — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":6300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Essence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: gain fly Speed equal to land Speed and resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier to the essence&#39;s one chosen energy type. Choose one type at creation from acid, cold, electricity or fire; no immunity is granted.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000064","name":"Runic Signature — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":6400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Runic Signature</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>While worn or held, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Arcana checks involving this artisan&#39;s sigils. Enable the Mark condition only for those sigils.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000065","name":"Resonant Pair — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":6500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Pair</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Link two paid items at creation. While both are worn or wielded within 30 feet, each bearer gains +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to saves against the last creature damaged by the other bearer this round. Track the eligible creature manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000066","name":"Layered Inscription — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":6600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Layered Inscription</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Choose one Standard Mark on this item and record three legal configurations of its existing choices. Switch one configuration during daily preparations; this does not grant all three benefits or bypass prerequisites.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000067","name":"Runic Feedback — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":6700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Runic Feedback</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Reaction, once per round when a linked weapon within 30 feet critically hits: its paired bearer gains +5 Artisan Bonus to their next attack or save before the end of their next turn. A bearer cannot trigger this from their own attack.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000068","name":"Living Rune — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":6800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Rune</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>One action, once per round: switch one Major-or-lower Mark between two recorded, equally costed configurations. Used charges and frequency limits remain spent across configurations; switching cannot refresh effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000069","name":"Grand Glyph — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":6900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Glyph</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Three actions, once per day: place a visible 20-foot-radius glyph within 60 feet for 1 minute. Allies in it gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to AC. Enemies starting turns inside take Core Tier d8 force damage, basic Reflex save against your higher class or spell DC. The glyph is stationary.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000070","name":"Flexible Construction — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":7000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Flexible Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Reduce this armor&#39;s land Speed penalty by 10 feet, minimum 0. It does not grant bonus Speed if the penalty is already absent.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000071","name":"Supple Gussets — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":7100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Supple Gussets</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Acrobatics checks to Squeeze. Physical passage size restrictions still apply.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000072","name":"Tanner's Acid Ward — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":7200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tanner&#39;s Acid Ward</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants acid resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. Resistance uses the highest applicable source, not their sum.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000073","name":"Weather Seal — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":7300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Weather Seal</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Fortitude saves against environmental heat, cold or exposure. Enable the Mark condition only for exposure, not energy attacks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000074","name":"Adaptive Strapping — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":7400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adaptive Strapping</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Once per round, draw or stow one strapped light item as part of an Interact action using that item. Also secure up to three such items against accidental loss; deliberate Disarm and theft are unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000075","name":"Wyrm Inscription — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":7500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Wyrm Inscription</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>The dragon&#39;s identity is visible on the item. While wielded or worn, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Arcana checks about that dragon type. Enable the Mark condition only for that subject.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000076","name":"Draconic Resistance — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":7600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Draconic Resistance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Add 3 × Dragon Tier to this item&#39;s native dragon resistance. This increases one resistance source, not all of the wearer&#39;s resistances.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000077","name":"Scale Dominion — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":7700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Scale Dominion</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Armor or shield gains +5 × Dragon Tier Hardness and +30 × Dragon Tier item HP. A weapon instead ignores 3 × Dragon Tier resistance against its associated dragon damage type; immunity remains.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Armor, Shield, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000078","name":"Draconic Constitution — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":7800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Draconic Constitution</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Worn armor grants +16 × Dragon Tier maximum HP and +5 Artisan Bonus to saves against its associated damage type; green scales apply to poison. Maximum HP is not healing.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000079","name":"Wyrm's Fury — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":7900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Wyrm&#39;s Fury</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Weapon gains +3 additional base weapon damage dice, using its existing die size and damage type. This Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000080","name":"Dragonheart Awakening — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":8000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dragonheart Awakening</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: gain fly Speed equal to twice land Speed and increase this item&#39;s native dragon resistance by 5 × Dragon Tier. Once during the duration, use two actions for a 30-foot cone dealing 3 × Dragon Tier d8 of the scale&#39;s damage type, basic Reflex against your higher class or spell DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal, Dragon Scale</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000081","name":"Trophy Memory — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":8100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Trophy Memory</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>While worn or wielded, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Nature checks to Recall Knowledge about the source creature family. Enable the Mark condition only for that family.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000082","name":"Predator's Sense — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":8200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predator&#39;s Sense</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>While worn, gain imprecise scent 30 feet and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Survival checks to Track the source creature family. Scent detects presence, not precise location; record the source family on the item.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000083","name":"Natural Movement — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":8300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Natural Movement</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Choose a source-appropriate climb or swim Speed at creation. Worn armor grants that Speed at 40 feet and +10 feet to land Speed in one recorded natural terrain. Terrain does not change during combat.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000084","name":"Apex Hide — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":8400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Apex Hide</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Worn armor grants +10 × Core Tier maximum HP and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Fortitude saves against one recorded creature theme: poison, cold or disease. This replaces the former start-of-combat temporary HP grant.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000085","name":"Apex Trait — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":8500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Apex Trait</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Worn armor grants imprecise tremorsense 30 feet while you share a solid surface with the target, and doubles your ordinary Leap distance. Tremorsense does not detect airborne creatures or bypass concealment.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000086","name":"Chimera Binding — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":8600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Chimera Binding</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Free action once per round: select one of two recorded creature-source senses or movement modes for this item. Once per day, both can be active for 10 minutes. Pay for both source components; no access to unrecorded creature abilities.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000087","name":"Trophy Finish — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":8700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Trophy Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Intimidation checks when the visible trophy is relevant to the audience. Enable the Mark condition only then; it is not mental control.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000088","name":"Whiteout Mantle — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":8800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Whiteout Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants cold resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier and an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to Survival. It does not grant weather immunity.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000089","name":"Predator's Cloak — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":8900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predator&#39;s Cloak</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth and Survival in one recorded terrain. Free action once per round after successfully Hiding there: Step up to 10 feet. The terrain must match the trophy&#39;s source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000090","name":"Court Mantle — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":9000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Court Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Diplomacy and Society in formal settings. Allies within 15 feet who can see you gain +3 Artisan Bonus to saves against fear while you are conscious; adjudicate the aura manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000091","name":"Dread Sovereign Pelt — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":9100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dread Sovereign Pelt</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Intimidation and Survival. A predator&#39;s presence dominates the hunt and the negotiation table without removing social consequences.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000092","name":"Legendary Pelt — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":9200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Legendary Pelt</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>One action, once per day for 1 minute: become invisible. After each hostile action the invisibility is suppressed until the start of your next turn. While invisible this way, gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth; invisibility is not undetectability.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000093","name":"Seasoned Construction — Carpentry — Universal","type":"text","sort":9300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Seasoned Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>Wooden armor or shield resists mundane warping and gains +100% of pre-Mark maximum item HP. This additive durability bonus does not multiply other Mark bonuses.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000094","name":"Light Frame — Carpentry — Universal","type":"text","sort":9400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Light Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>Reduce Bulk by 2, minimum 0, when the wooden frame forms most of this item. Contents and attached equipment retain their own Bulk.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000095","name":"Precision Joinery — Carpentry — Universal","type":"text","sort":9500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Precision Joinery</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>While held or worn, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Crafting checks to Repair this item or operate its mechanism. Enable the Mark condition only for that mechanism.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000096","name":"Skyhunter Limbs — Carpentry — Universal","type":"text","sort":9600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Skyhunter Limbs</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>A ranged weapon deals +3 × Core Tier damage against flying or falling targets. Enable the Mark condition only against an airborne target.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000097","name":"Modular Frame — Carpentry — Universal","type":"text","sort":9700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Modular Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>During daily preparations replace up to three ordinary wooden components with paid compatible alternatives. Retain legal Marks and maker records; no free resources, Capacity or extra active Core progression.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000098","name":"True Fletching — Carpentry — Warbowyer","type":"text","sort":9800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>True Fletching</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to attacks affected by ordinary wind. Enable the Mark condition only during such wind. Magical wind and range penalties remain.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000099","name":"Specialist Ammo Chamber — Carpentry — Warbowyer","type":"text","sort":9900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Specialist Ammo Chamber</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Ranged weapon accepts two recorded compatible specialist ammunition families. Ammunition is paid and consumed normally; this does not enable ammunition of the wrong weapon category.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000100","name":"Longshot Construction — Carpentry — Warbowyer","type":"text","sort":10000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Longshot Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Double this ranged weapon&#39;s range increment. Normal increment penalties and line of effect still apply; this does not increase melee reach.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000101","name":"Rapid Mechanism — Carpentry — Warbowyer","type":"text","sort":10100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Rapid Mechanism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Free action once per round: reload this ranged weapon by up to two Interact actions. Supply ammunition and a free hand normally. A reload-0 weapon instead gains +5 Artisan Bonus to its next Strike this turn; these options are exclusive.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000102","name":"Horizonstring — Carpentry — Warbowyer","type":"text","sort":10200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Horizonstring</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>A ranged weapon grants +2 Artisan Bonus to attacks against targets beyond its first range increment. This Over-Potency bonus is capped at +2 per Mark. Enable the Mark condition only at that distance. Normal range penalties still apply.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000103","name":"Warbow Overdraw — Carpentry — Warbowyer","type":"text","sort":10300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Warbow Overdraw</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +3 additional base weapon damage dice using its own die size and type. After a natural 1 on a Strike, you are off-guard until the start of your next turn. Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000104","name":"Builder's Mark — Carpentry — Masterwright","type":"text","sort":10400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Builder&#39;s Mark</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Inspecting this wooden construction grants +Core Tier + 2 to Crafting checks to identify weaknesses or plan repairs. The mark records load paths; no actor effect is created.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000105","name":"Reinforced Frame — Carpentry — Masterwright","type":"text","sort":10500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reinforced Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Wooden structure or vehicle gains ×3 pre-Mark maximum HP and +4 × Core Tier Hardness. Other durability bonuses add from the same base rather than compounding.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000106","name":"Rapid Assembly — Carpentry — Masterwright","type":"text","sort":10600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Rapid Assembly</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Qualifying construction or field fortification takes half its original artisan-days, minimum one. Apply once to original work, not recursively after other reductions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000107","name":"Modular Construction — Carpentry — Masterwright","type":"text","sort":10700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Modular Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Recover 90% of recorded ordinary inputs when dismantling, rounded down; unique inputs require GM adjudication. Re-deploy the stored modules in one-quarter normal assembly time, minimum 10 minutes.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000108","name":"Grand Design — Carpentry — Masterwright","type":"text","sort":10800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Design</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Choose recurring Lumber or repair cost: reduce it by 40%, minimum one unit. Gain +5 on the structure&#39;s principal construction check. These are campaign project benefits, not character Crafting bonuses.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000109","name":"Citadel Framework — Carpentry — Masterwright","type":"text","sort":10900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Citadel Framework</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Defenders gain +5 to checks and saves against forced entry, collapse and siege movement while within the fortification. Gates and walls gain structural damage resistance equal to 8 × Core Tier.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000110","name":"Carved Grip — Carpentry — Warcarving","type":"text","sort":11000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Carved Grip</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 to your DC against Disarm attempts targeting this weapon. It does not protect other held items or prevent voluntary dropping.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000111","name":"Wolf Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","type":"text","sort":11100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Wolf Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Free action once per round after this weapon hits: Stride up to half Speed toward that target. Movement must end closer and triggers reactions normally.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000112","name":"Bear Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","type":"text","sort":11200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Bear Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>While the shield is raised, gain physical resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier; against damage caused by forced movement, use 6 × Core Tier instead. Use only the applicable value, not both.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000113","name":"Serpent Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","type":"text","sort":11300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Serpent Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Weapon gains +5 feet melee reach. Free action once per round after hitting: Step up to 15 feet; this movement does not trigger that target&#39;s reactions. Other creatures react normally if applicable.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000114","name":"Spirit Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","type":"text","sort":11400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Spirit Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>One action, once per encounter for 1 minute: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to this weapon&#39;s attacks and imprecise scent 30 feet. This is a magical spirit manifestation; it grants no extra actions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000115","name":"Totemic Ascendance — Carpentry — Warcarving","type":"text","sort":11500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Totemic Ascendance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Athletics, +20 feet land Speed and resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier to physical damage. A visible animal spirit surrounds the wearer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000116","name":"Stonebound — Stonemasonry — Universal","type":"text","sort":11600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stonebound</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>Armor or shield gains +50% of its pre-Mark maximum item HP and +2 × Core Tier Hardness. The stone protects the item, not its wearer&#39;s HP. Durability bonuses add against the same pre-Mark base.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000117","name":"Perfect Foundation — Stonemasonry — Universal","type":"text","sort":11700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Foundation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on checks to stabilise or repair a structure built on this foundation. Its reference lines reveal subsidence before ordinary collapse.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000118","name":"Anchored Construction — Stonemasonry — Universal","type":"text","sort":11800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Anchored Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>Structure gains +Core Tier + 2 to its DC against forced movement or toppling and counts as two sizes larger for those contests. It can still be damaged or destroyed.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000119","name":"Load-Bearing Cut — Stonemasonry — Universal","type":"text","sort":11900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Load-Bearing Cut</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>Stone structure gains +100% of pre-Mark maximum HP. This adds to other durability bonuses using the same base; it does not grant character HP.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000120","name":"Resonant Stone — Stonemasonry — Universal","type":"text","sort":12000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Stone</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>The component can provide both ward and arcane-anchor tags for compatible work. Tags grant eligibility only, not extra Capacity, Core progression or free Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000121","name":"Mason's Seal — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","type":"text","sort":12100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mason&#39;s Seal</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on Crafting checks to identify damage, load paths or reconstruction methods in the sealed stonework. Inspection reveals non-magical hidden cavities within 5 feet of the examined surface.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000122","name":"Enduring Monument — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","type":"text","sort":12200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Enduring Monument</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Monument has ×4 pre-Mark maximum HP and +5 × Core Tier Hardness. Durability bonuses add from the pre-Mark base rather than multiplying one another.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000123","name":"Grand Foundation — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","type":"text","sort":12300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Foundation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Structures on this foundation gain +5 against collapse, subsidence and siege movement. Repairs restore twice normal item HP without consuming additional ordinary repair materials.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000124","name":"Civic Wonder — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","type":"text","sort":12400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Civic Wonder</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Choose Culture, Defence, Trade, Faith or Infrastructure at creation. Once per Kingdom turn gain +5 on one project check directly serving that purpose. The wonder also acts as a recognised landmark; no automatic income is created.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000125","name":"Imperial Work — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","type":"text","sort":12500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Imperial Work</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Reduce one named recurring Kingdom resource cost tied to this structure by 40%, minimum one unit. Once per Kingdom turn reroll one failed maintenance check for it and use the new result.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000126","name":"World-Rooted Foundation — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","type":"text","sort":12600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>World-Rooted Foundation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>The structure cannot be moved or toppled by non-magical effects. It gains structural damage resistance equal to 12 × Core Tier; magical displacement requires a counteract check against the completed project&#39;s recorded DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000127","name":"Inscribed Keystone — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","type":"text","sort":12700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Inscribed Keystone</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on checks to identify or repair this ward. Authorised users can read its owner, purpose and whether it has been breached.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000128","name":"Sentinel Rune — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","type":"text","sort":12800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sentinel Rune</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>Detect a recorded creature trait crossing the site&#39;s boundary within 300 feet of the rune. Alert up to six designated creatures anywhere inside the site; this is an alarm, not precise tracking or a hostile effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000129","name":"Sanctuary Ward — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","type":"text","sort":12900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sanctuary Ward</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>A stationary 30-foot zone grants authorised allies +5 to saves while inside. Once per creature per day on entering, restore 10 × Core Tier HP. Leaving and re-entering does not refresh healing.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000130","name":"War Rune — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","type":"text","sort":13000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>War Rune</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>In a stationary 30-foot zone, authorised defenders gain +5 to attack rolls and +3 × Core Tier damage on their first successful Strike each round. The rune does not move with a bearer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000131","name":"Fortress Sigil — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","type":"text","sort":13100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Fortress Sigil</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>Hostile teleportation or planar entry into the recorded site requires a counteract check against the project&#39;s recorded DC +5. Failure prevents entry and spends the attempt normally; authorised travel is unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000132","name":"Dominion Ward — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","type":"text","sort":13200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dominion Ward</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>One recorded hostile creature trait suffers -5 to attacks and saves within a 60-foot ward. Those creatures cannot use ordinary concealment against authorised defenders; invisibility and total cover remain unless separately overcome.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Structure</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000133","name":"Titanic Fit — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","type":"text","sort":13300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Titanic Fit</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Ignore up to 3 Bulk belonging to this stone item while properly worn or wielded, minimum 0. Contents and other equipment are unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000134","name":"Anchored — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","type":"text","sort":13400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Anchored</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>While worn or raised, gain +5 to the DC against Trip or Reposition and count as two sizes larger for resisting forced movement. This does not increase your actual size or offensive manoeuvre limits.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000135","name":"Earthshaker — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","type":"text","sort":13500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Earthshaker</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Free action once per round after a critical weapon hit or successful Shield Block: choose an adjacent enemy. Fortitude against your higher class/spell DC: failure pushes it 10 feet and makes it off-guard until the end of its next turn; critical failure also knocks it prone. No effect on success.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000136","name":"Basalt Bastion — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","type":"text","sort":13600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Basalt Bastion</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier and an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to Fortitude saves.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000137","name":"Heart of the Mountain — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","type":"text","sort":13700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Heart of the Mountain</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier, an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Fortitude saves, and -5 feet to land Speed. Physical resistances use the highest source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000138","name":"Living Colossus — Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry","type":"text","sort":13800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Colossus</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: grow one size category, gain +10 feet melee reach, +5 Artisan Bonus to Athletics and physical resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier. End in sufficient space; equipment enlarges but its sale value and permanent Bulk do not change.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000139","name":"Perfect Clarity — Glassmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":13900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Clarity</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>A held optic grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Perception checks involving visual detail. Enable the Mark condition only when viewing through the optic; it does not bypass concealment. Stored Flare — Three actions (Concentrate, Manipulate, Light), once per day: release stored light in a 15-foot emanation. Creatures other than you attempt a Fortitude save against your higher class or spell DC: failure dazzled for Core Tier rounds; critical failure blinded for 1 round, then dazzled for Core Tier rounds; success unaffected. Resolve saves and conditions manually. This is a visual effect.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000140","name":"Glarecut Glass — Glassmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":14000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Glarecut Glass</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>A held focus grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to visual Seek checks. Enable the Mark condition when sight applies; concealment is not negated.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000141","name":"Arcane Lens — Glassmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":14100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Lens</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>The optical component grants arcane, optic and conductor tags and can provide two compatible lens sockets. Supply their materials and Marks normally; no Capacity increase.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000142","name":"Precision Focus — Glassmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":14200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Precision Focus</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to attacks against a target you successfully Sought this turn using the mounted optic. Enable the Mark condition only for that target and turn. Prismatic Sightline — Two actions, once per encounter: Seek using the optic, then make one ranged Strike with this weapon against a creature you detected. Ignore ordinary concealment for that Strike, but not hidden, undetected or total cover. Normal multiple attack penalty applies.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000143","name":"Shatter Safe — Glassmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":14300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shatter Safe</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Universal</p><p>Twice per day when damage would destroy this glass-bearing item, it instead remains at 1 item HP. This protects the item only; worn-item protection does not prevent bearer damage. Record spent uses manually. Shatter Ward — Reaction. Trigger: damage would destroy this item. Spend one of this Mark&#39;s two daily uses to leave it at 1 item HP instead. This is the activation cost of its existing protection, not additional uses; it never prevents damage to the bearer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000144","name":"Surveyor's Reticle — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","type":"text","sort":14400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Surveyor&#39;s Reticle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>A held focus grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to initiative. Read the battlefield before the first blow.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000145","name":"Focusing Lens — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","type":"text","sort":14500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Focusing Lens</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>Increase the ranged weapon&#39;s range increment by 50%. The mounted optical sight does not affect melee reach or remove range penalties.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000146","name":"Spectrum Prism — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","type":"text","sort":14600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Spectrum Prism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>Choose two energy types from acid, cold, electricity or fire at creation. Free action once per round before this weapon&#39;s Strike: convert all its added energy damage from the first type to the second, or back. Base physical damage is unchanged.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000147","name":"Beam Splitter — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","type":"text","sort":14700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Beam Splitter</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>Reaction, once per encounter after a ranged weapon Strike hits: make a second Strike against a different target within 30 feet of the first, using the same multiple attack penalty as the triggering Strike. This additional Strike counts toward later attacks; pay ammunition normally.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon, Ranged Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000148","name":"Trueglass Crown — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","type":"text","sort":14800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Trueglass Crown</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>Worn armor reveals invisible creatures to you within 60 feet as concealed rather than invisible. Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves against visual illusions. It does not see through walls or automatically disbelieve illusions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000149","name":"Sovereign Refraction — Glassmaking — Prismcraft","type":"text","sort":14900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sovereign Refraction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Prismcraft</p><p>A held spell focus grants +2 Artisan Bonus to spell DC and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Arcana, with a -1 Artisan spell-attack penalty. The Over-Potency spell DC bonus is capped at +2 per Mark. Requires a Tier 5+ optical Anchor. Its power favours save spells.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000150","name":"Perfect Reflection — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","type":"text","sort":15000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Reflection</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>A held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Deception checks to Impersonate using the mirror to prepare your disguise. Enable the Mark condition only for that prepared disguise.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000151","name":"Truth Mirror — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","type":"text","sort":15100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Truth Mirror</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>A held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Perception checks to Sense Motive or detect a visual disguise through the mirror. Enable the Mark condition only for those checks; no automatic lie detection. Unmask — One action, once per encounter: attempt to counteract one visual illusion affecting a creature or object seen through the mirror within 30 feet. Use your higher class or spell DC minus 10 for the counteract modifier and Core Tier as counteract rank. Ordinary disguises instead permit one immediate Seek check.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000152","name":"Reflective Ward — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","type":"text","sort":15200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reflective Ward</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>Reaction, once per encounter when a spell attack targets you: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to AC against that attack. If it critically misses, deal Core Tier d8 force damage to its caster within 60 feet, basic Reflex against your higher class/spell DC. This is retaliation, not a copied spell.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000153","name":"Doppelglass — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","type":"text","sort":15300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Doppelglass</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>One action, once per encounter: gain concealed until the start of your next turn. The first attack that misses because of this flat check lets you Step 10 feet as a free action; this movement does not end the concealment.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000154","name":"Gate Mirror — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","type":"text","sort":15400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Gate Mirror</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>Three actions, once per day: open a two-way portal between this mirror and its paid, attuned partner within 10 miles on the same plane for 1 minute. Up to six willing creatures may cross. Both exits require open space; dimensional wards can block passage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000155","name":"Mirror Lord — Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft","type":"text","sort":15500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mirror Lord</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: once per round use your reaction when targeted by a spell attack to counteract it using your higher class/spell DC minus 10 and counteract rank equal to Core Tier. Success negates it; critical success also deals 2 × Core Tier d8 force damage to the caster, basic Reflex against that DC.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000156","name":"Stable Cell — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","type":"text","sort":15600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stable Cell</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Recorded magical charges cannot decay from ordinary time or environmental exposure. Once per day ignore one effect that would drain a single charge; this does not stop deliberate use or regenerate spent charges.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000157","name":"Mana Reservoir — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","type":"text","sort":15700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mana Reservoir</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Add three daily charges to one named custom activation on this item. Charges cannot fuel recovery, extra-charge or refresh effects and return only at daily preparations. Reservoir Lance — Two actions, once per encounter: expend one charge from the named pool to deal 2 × Core Tier d6 force damage to one creature within 60 feet, basic Reflex against your higher class or spell DC. This does not restore or create charges; resolve damage and charge spending manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000158","name":"Arcane Conductor — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","type":"text","sort":15800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Conductor</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Weapon gains +2 additional base weapon damage dice from a luminous glass channel. Use its existing die size and type; this Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000159","name":"Overflow Channel — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","type":"text","sort":15900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Overflow Channel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Free action once per encounter before a damaging item activation: add Core Tier d8 damage of that activation&#39;s primary damage type. If it costs charges, pay one additional charge. Applies once to one damage roll, not persistent or repeated damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000160","name":"Crystal Matrix — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","type":"text","sort":16000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Crystal Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Reduce the Capacity cost of one compatible paid Enchanting or Azlanti Artifice Mark by 2, minimum 1. Does not grant a free Mark or raise maximum Capacity. Multiple discounts apply to the original cost, never below 1.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000161","name":"Eternity Cell — Glassmaking — Aetherglass","type":"text","sort":16100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Eternity Cell</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Glassmaking — Aetherglass</p><p>Add five charges per day to one named custom activation. Once per encounter when you critically succeed at an attack or save, recover one charge spent on that activation. Cannot fuel charge generation, resource recovery, healing or refresh effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lens, catalyst, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000162","name":"Emberproof Glaze — Pottery — Universal","type":"text","sort":16200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Emberproof Glaze</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>Worn armor or a held shield grants fire resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. Resistance uses the highest applicable source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000163","name":"Thermal Craft — Pottery — Universal","type":"text","sort":16300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Thermal Craft</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>Contents remain at their stored mundane temperature for 24 hours while sealed. The vessel ignores ordinary heat/cold damage from storage; attacks, spells and bearer damage are unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000164","name":"Sealed Vessel — Pottery — Universal","type":"text","sort":16400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sealed Vessel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>Contents cannot leak, evaporate or become mundanely contaminated until the vessel is destroyed, not merely Broken. Does not preserve a consumed dose or increase storage capacity.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000165","name":"Shock-Fired — Pottery — Universal","type":"text","sort":16500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shock-Fired</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>The ceramic item gains +Core Tier + 2 to its DC or checks against shattering and rupture effects. This is item protection, not a bonus to the bearer&#39;s saves.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000166","name":"Nested Chamber — Pottery — Universal","type":"text","sort":16600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Nested Chamber</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Universal</p><p>Add three concealed internal chambers, each holding one light dose or object. Their contents count toward Bulk; searching the chambers uses the normal concealment rules with +Core Tier + 2 to the item&#39;s concealment DC. Chamber Draw — One action (Manipulate): retrieve one object from a chamber into a free hand. This does not activate, drink or use the retrieved object; those actions retain their normal costs.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000167","name":"Fired Seal — Pottery — Ceramancy","type":"text","sort":16700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Fired Seal</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>While worn or held, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Crafting checks to Repair or identify this ceramic item. Enable the Mark condition only when working on this item.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000168","name":"Ceramic Plate — Pottery — Ceramancy","type":"text","sort":16800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Ceramic Plate</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>Armor or shield gains +5 × Core Tier Hardness and +40 × Core Tier item HP without increased Bulk. This improves the item, not wearer maximum HP. Kiln Renewal — Two actions, once per encounter: touch the armor or shield to restore 8 × Core Tier item HP, up to its maximum. It must not be destroyed. This repairs the item, never its wearer&#39;s HP.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000169","name":"Living Clay — Pottery — Ceramancy","type":"text","sort":16900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Clay</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>At the start of the wearer&#39;s turn during an encounter, repair this item for 5 × Core Tier HP if it is not destroyed. Outside encounters it repairs once per minute. It cannot restore missing components or the wearer&#39;s HP.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor, Shield</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000170","name":"Terracotta Guardian — Pottery — Ceramancy","type":"text","sort":17000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Terracotta Guardian</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>Three actions, once per day: animate a guardian for 1 minute using a creature stat block recorded at creation, maximum level equal to twice Core Tier. It has the minion trait and requires one action to command; no independent extra turns or summoning abilities. The GM approves the exact stat block.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000171","name":"Adaptive Ceramic — Pottery — Ceramancy","type":"text","sort":17100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adaptive Ceramic</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>Reaction once per round before taking bludgeoning, piercing or slashing damage: gain resistance equal to 6 × Core Tier against that type, including the triggering damage, until the start of your next turn. Other physical types are unaffected.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000172","name":"Living Ceramic Shell — Pottery — Ceramancy","type":"text","sort":17200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Ceramic Shell</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Ceramancy</p><p>Worn armor grants +20 × Core Tier maximum HP. At the start of each encounter turn repair the armor itself for 4 × Core Tier item HP. Replaces regenerating temporary HP; removing or re-equipping grants no healing.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000173","name":"Sanctified Vessel — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","type":"text","sort":17300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sanctified Vessel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>While holding the vessel, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Religion checks to identify its contained essence. Enable the Mark condition for that essence only. Mundane spiritual leakage is prevented.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000174","name":"Essence Vessel — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","type":"text","sort":17400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Essence Vessel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>Store up to three separately sealed harvested essences without ordinary degradation. They remain distinct paid inputs; opening one chamber does not consume or expose the others.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000175","name":"Bound Spirit — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","type":"text","sort":17500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Bound Spirit</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>Record a willing spirit and one Lore at creation. While holding the vessel gain +5 Artisan Bonus to checks with that Lore; the spirit can speak to its bearer. It grants neither extra turns nor access to undisclosed creature abilities.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000176","name":"Sealed Curse — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","type":"text","sort":17600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sealed Curse</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>A successfully contained curse cannot spread while this vessel remains intact. Gain +5 on attempts to counteract the contained curse using the normal counteract procedure. The containment itself requires resolving the curse, not simply placing this Mark.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000177","name":"Release Matrix — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","type":"text","sort":17700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Release Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>Two actions, once per day: discharge one paid stored essence in a 30-foot cone for 3 × Core Tier d8 spirit damage, basic Will against your higher class/spell DC. Consume the essence; recharging requires another compatible harvested essence.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000178","name":"Grand Reliquary — Pottery — Reliquarycraft","type":"text","sort":17800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Reliquary</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Reliquarycraft</p><p>Hold three paid compatible essences. Two actions once per day: consume two to heal up to six willing creatures within 30 feet for 8 × Core Tier HP each and reduce their frightened by 2. Refilling does not reset the daily use.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000179","name":"Heatproof Glaze — Pottery — Pyroceramics","type":"text","sort":17900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Heatproof Glaze</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>The vessel ignores ordinary forge heat and gains +Core Tier + 2 to checks against magical thermal breakage. This does not protect the bearer from fire damage or create a resistance aura.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000180","name":"Thermal Crucible — Pottery — Pyroceramics","type":"text","sort":18000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Thermal Crucible</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>When processing heat-sensitive ordinary materials, recover 30% of otherwise lost units, rounded down. Recovery cannot exceed recorded loss and cannot be recycled through the same process for new material.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000181","name":"Fragmenting Casing — Pottery — Pyroceramics","type":"text","sort":18100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Fragmenting Casing</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>A bomb gains 10 feet additional splash radius and +3 × Core Tier splash damage. Allies in the enlarged area are affected normally; do not multiply direct-hit damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000182","name":"Shaped Charge — Pottery — Pyroceramics","type":"text","sort":18200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shaped Charge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>On use choose concentrated detonation: remove all splash damage and add Core Tier d12 primary damage against the directly hit creature or object. A miss does not deal this additional damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000183","name":"Pressure Vessel — Pottery — Pyroceramics","type":"text","sort":18300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Pressure Vessel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>Multiply the explosive&#39;s base primary damage dice by 3. Do not multiply flat bonuses, splash, persistent damage or added Mark dice. A critical manufacturing failure destroys the paid ordinary casing inputs.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000184","name":"Furnace Heart — Pottery — Pyroceramics","type":"text","sort":18400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Furnace Heart</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Pottery — Pyroceramics</p><p>Two actions, once per day: a 20-foot emanation deals 3 × Core Tier d8 fire damage to other creatures, basic Reflex against your higher class/spell DC. The item also serves as a portable forge for downtime when set down safely.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, reagent</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000185","name":"Lightweave — Weaving — Universal","type":"text","sort":18500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Lightweave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>Reduce this primarily textile item&#39;s Bulk by 2, minimum 0. This does not reduce the Bulk of its contents or other carried equipment.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Universal</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000186","name":"Perfect Thread — Weaving — Universal","type":"text","sort":18600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Thread</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on the next Tailoring or Leatherwork project check that consumes this textile. Once consumed, the thread cannot grant this benefit to a second project.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000187","name":"Slipknot Weave — Weaving — Universal","type":"text","sort":18700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Slipknot Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Athletics and Acrobatics checks to Escape, not unarmed Escape attacks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000188","name":"Weatherproof Weave — Weaving — Universal","type":"text","sort":18800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Weatherproof Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>Worn armor ignores ordinary rain exposure and grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Fortitude saves against severe non-magical weather. Enable the Mark condition only for weather.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000189","name":"Tensioned Thread — Weaving — Universal","type":"text","sort":18900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tensioned Thread</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Universal</p><p>A woven weapon gains +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Athletics checks to Grapple or Trip with it. Enable the Mark condition only when using that weapon, and it must already have the relevant trait.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000190","name":"Resonant Thread — Weaving — Aetherweaving","type":"text","sort":19000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Thread</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Textile supplies mana, conductor and aetherwoven tags for compatible work. Its visible pattern grants +Core Tier + 2 to identify its own magic; it does not add free Marks or spell slots.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000191","name":"Manaweave — Weaving — Aetherweaving","type":"text","sort":19100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Manaweave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier to one chosen acid, cold, electricity or fire type. Use the highest applicable resistance source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000192","name":"Spellthread — Weaving — Aetherweaving","type":"text","sort":19200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Spellthread</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Two actions once per day: restore 6 × Core Tier HP to one willing touched creature and let it immediately Step up to 10 feet. This is a magical restoration activation, not a stored spell slot.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000193","name":"Ethereal Weave — Weaving — Aetherweaving","type":"text","sort":19300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Ethereal Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Ignore non-magical ground difficult terrain while wearing this armor. Free action once per encounter: Step up to 20 feet through occupied creature spaces, ending in an open space. Does not pass through walls.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000194","name":"Expanded Matrix — Weaving — Aetherweaving","type":"text","sort":19400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Expanded Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Reduce the Capacity cost of one compatible paid Enchanting or Tailoring Mark by 2, minimum 1. Total costs still cannot exceed Core Capacity. Discounts apply to the original cost, not recursively.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000195","name":"Aetherbound Form — Weaving — Aetherweaving","type":"text","sort":19500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Aetherbound Form</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Aetherweaving</p><p>Two actions once per day for 1 minute: gain fly Speed 40 feet, physical resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier, and squeeze through openings as though two sizes smaller. You are not incorporeal and cannot pass through solid walls.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000196","name":"Warcloth Finish — Weaving — Ironweaving","type":"text","sort":19600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Warcloth Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Textile armor gains +100% of pre-Mark maximum item HP. This does not increase wearer HP; other durability bonuses use the same original base.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000197","name":"Impact Mesh — Weaving — Ironweaving","type":"text","sort":19700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Impact Mesh</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. Resistance does not add to other physical-resistance sources. Impact Lock — Two actions, once per encounter: until the start of your next turn, increase this Mark&#39;s physical resistance to 6 × Core Tier. This replaces its passive resistance for that duration; do not add the two together. Resolve the temporary increase manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000198","name":"Flexible Weave — Weaving — Ironweaving","type":"text","sort":19800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Flexible Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Reduce this armor&#39;s land Speed penalty by 15 feet, minimum 0, and raise its Dexterity modifier cap by 3. This changes the armor cap, not your Dexterity score.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000199","name":"Shock-Absorbing Warcloth — Weaving — Ironweaving","type":"text","sort":19900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shock-Absorbing Warcloth</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants +12 × Core Tier maximum HP. This replaces per-turn temporary HP; it does not heal when equipped or grant damage absorption beyond the maximum-HP increase.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000200","name":"Silken Steel — Weaving — Ironweaving","type":"text","sort":20000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Silken Steel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants +5 Artisan Bonus to AC beyond Core progression and physical resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier. AC stacks with different Marks; resistance uses the highest source.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000201","name":"Lifeline Braid — Weaving — Ironweaving","type":"text","sort":20100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Lifeline Braid</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Ironweaving</p><p>Worn armor grants bleed resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier and an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Athletics and Acrobatics checks to Escape, not unarmed Escape attacks.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000202","name":"Heraldic Seal — Weaving — Heraldweaving","type":"text","sort":20200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Heraldic Seal</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society checks proving the authority or affiliation displayed by this worn armor. Enable the Mark condition only where that affiliation matters.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000203","name":"Unbroken Standard — Weaving — Heraldweaving","type":"text","sort":20300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Unbroken Standard</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>While this focus is held and displayed, allies within 30 feet who can see it gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to saves against fear. The bearer must be conscious; resolve recipients manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000204","name":"Marching Banner — Weaving — Heraldweaving","type":"text","sort":20400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Marching Banner</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Allies starting their turns within 30 feet of the displayed focus gain +15 feet Artisan land Speed for that turn and ignore the first 15 feet of difficult terrain. Does not grant extra actions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000205","name":"King's Colours — Weaving — Heraldweaving","type":"text","sort":20500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>King&#39;s Colours</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Allies within 30 feet of the displayed focus gain +5 Artisan Bonus to Aid checks and saves against mental effects while they can see its conscious bearer.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000206","name":"Conqueror's Standard — Weaving — Heraldweaving","type":"text","sort":20600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Conqueror&#39;s Standard</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Two actions once per encounter for 1 minute: when an ally within 30 feet reduces a hostile creature to 0 HP, that ally gains +5 Artisan Bonus to attacks until the end of its next turn. Multiple defeats refresh duration, not bonus magnitude.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000207","name":"Sovereign Standard — Weaving — Heraldweaving","type":"text","sort":20700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sovereign Standard</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Weaving — Heraldweaving</p><p>Two actions once per day for 1 minute: allies within 30 feet gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves and +3 × Core Tier damage on their first hit each round. On activation grant each ally a separately tracked 10-point Artisan temporary-HP buffer, expiring after 1 minute. Do not overwrite class temporary HP; record and deduct the buffer manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000208","name":"Perfect Index — Bookmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":20800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Index</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>Find any recorded entry in this held focus immediately. Gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society checks to Recall Knowledge directly documented in it; enable the Mark condition only for that subject.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000209","name":"Preserved Knowledge — Bookmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":20900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Preserved Knowledge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>The work is immune to mundane water, ageing and mildew. A legible copy of damaged pages can be restored during one hour of study if at least half the original survives; it does not recover erased magical secrets.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000210","name":"Master Copy — Bookmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":21000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Master Copy</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>Copy a paid formula or mundane text in one-quarter normal downtime, minimum 10 minutes. Material and licence costs remain; copying does not duplicate magic, consumables or activation charges.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000211","name":"Encoded Script — Bookmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":21100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Encoded Script</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 to the DC to Decipher Writing in this focus without its key. Authorised readers can read normally; possession of a stolen key bypasses the encoding.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000212","name":"Reference Tabs — Bookmaking — Universal","type":"text","sort":21200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reference Tabs</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Universal</p><p>Free action once per 10 minutes before Recall Knowledge using this held focus&#39;s recorded subject: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to that check. No benefit on an undocumented subject.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000213","name":"Indexed Arcana — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","type":"text","sort":21300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Indexed Arcana</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Arcana checks about spells recorded in it. Enable the Mark condition only for those spells; the index locates their entries immediately.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000214","name":"Mnemonic Pages — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","type":"text","sort":21400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mnemonic Pages</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Once per day after 10 minutes of study, replace up to three unexpended prepared spells with known spells of the same ranks. Does not restore spent slots or grant spells the reader cannot normally prepare.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000215","name":"Resonant Chapter — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","type":"text","sort":21500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Chapter</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Choose one spell trait at creation. Spells with that trait gain +3 damage per spell rank on their first damage roll against each target. This is flat bonus damage, not multiplied ongoing damage; record the chosen trait.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000216","name":"Spell Echo — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","type":"text","sort":21600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Spell Echo</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Reaction once per encounter after a spell deals damage to one target: deal additional damage equal to Core Tier d8 of its primary type to that target or a second creature within 15 feet. Basic Reflex against your spell DC. This is a separate magical echo and cannot echo itself.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000217","name":"Archmage Codex — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","type":"text","sort":21700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Archmage Codex</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Elemental Thesis — Choose Acid, Cold, Electricity, Fire or Sonic when applying this Mark. While holding this spell focus, damaging spells bearing the chosen elemental trait gain bonus damage of that type. Passive formula: 2 × spell damage die (3 × at Core Tier 6). Ascendant Thesis — Two actions, once per encounter for 1 minute: replace the passive bonus with (Core Tier + 2) × spell damage die. Use the chosen type&#39;s first base damage component and its largest die; if that type is absent, use the spell&#39;s first base component. Flat-only components provide no bonus dice. Example: Core Tier 4 with a d6 spell adds 2d6 passively or 6d6 while activated. Add this once to initial damage, not each missile, persistent tick or later repeated damage. Enable Initial Spell Damage only for that roll. Enable Ascendant Thesis after activation and clear it when the minute ends. Uses and duration are tracked manually; active and passive dice never add together.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000218","name":"Endless Grimoire — Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft","type":"text","sort":21800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Endless Grimoire</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft</p><p>Three actions once per day: recover one expended spell slot of rank no higher than Core Tier, maximum 6. It cannot recover a slot used to create permanent resources, restore slots or activate another recovery effect. Non-slot casters require a recorded equivalent before crafting.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>3 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000219","name":"Scholar's Index — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","type":"text","sort":21900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Scholar&#39;s Index</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>Held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society research checks on its documented subject. Enable the Mark condition only during that research.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000220","name":"Lore Codex — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","type":"text","sort":22000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Lore Codex</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>After 10 minutes study choose one recorded narrow Lore. Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to checks with that Lore for 8 hours, even if untrained, but do not gain proficiency ranks or trained-only actions.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000221","name":"Crafting Manual — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","type":"text","sort":22100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Crafting Manual</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>For one recorded recipe family reduce required artisan-days by 40%, minimum one, and gain +5 to its first project check each day. Reductions use original work; this does not create free materials.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000222","name":"Tactical Treatise — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","type":"text","sort":22200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tactical Treatise</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>Free action once per encounter before an attack, save or Recall Knowledge against a documented creature trait: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to that roll. The trait is chosen at creation and must match the target.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000223","name":"Master's Testament — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","type":"text","sort":22300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Master&#39;s Testament</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>During daily preparations choose one of three recorded skill feats whose level and other prerequisites you meet. Gain its use until next preparations. No ancestry, class, dedication or spellcasting feats; it cannot grant crafting outputs retroactively.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000224","name":"Legendary Chronicle — Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft","type":"text","sort":22400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Legendary Chronicle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft</p><p>Up to six readers study for 10 minutes during daily preparations. Each gains +5 Artisan Bonus to one recorded narrow Lore for the day and one fortune reroll of a failed check with that Lore, using the new result. Restudying does not reset uses.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000225","name":"Surveyor's Mark — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","type":"text","sort":22500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Surveyor&#39;s Mark</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>Held map grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Survival checks to navigate its recorded territory. Enable the Mark condition only within mapped territory.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000226","name":"Safe Passage — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","type":"text","sort":22600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Safe Passage</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>In mapped territory reduce travel delays from documented non-magical hazards by 50%. Does not increase encounter Speed, remove hazards outright or reduce an undelayed journey.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000227","name":"Resource Survey — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","type":"text","sort":22700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resource Survey</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>A successful survey reveals one hidden ordinary resource site and grants +5 on the first extraction check there each Kingdom turn. No resource is created without a site; unique discoveries remain GM-controlled.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000228","name":"Strategic Map — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","type":"text","sort":22800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Strategic Map</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>Held map grants +5 Artisan Bonus to initiative in its recorded region when studied for 10 minutes earlier that day. Enable the Mark condition only within the studied region.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Spell Focus</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000229","name":"Hidden Paths — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","type":"text","sort":22900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Hidden Paths</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>Establish a mapped secret route: travel along it takes half normal non-combat time and travellers gain +5 to avoid detection on the route. It cannot cross impassable terrain or ignore hostile fortifications.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000230","name":"World Atlas — Bookmaking — Grand Cartography","type":"text","sort":23000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>World Atlas</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Bookmaking — Grand Cartography</p><p>At each Kingdom turn choose one mapped region: double ordinary resource output, halve ordinary travel time, or gain +5 on settlement-planning checks there for that turn. Only one mode applies; never duplicate unique or story resources.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, cover, catalyst</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000231","name":"Tailored First Impression — Tailoring — Universal","type":"text","sort":23100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tailored First Impression</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Diplomacy checks to Make an Impression. This does not compel agreement or bypass attitudes.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000232","name":"Steadfast Hem — Tailoring — Universal","type":"text","sort":23200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Steadfast Hem</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to Will saves against fear. Enable the Mark condition only against fear effects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000233","name":"Hidden Pocketing — Tailoring — Universal","type":"text","sort":23300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Hidden Pocketing</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Thievery checks to Conceal an Object in its fitted pockets. Enable the Mark condition only for an object that fits; Bulk is unchanged.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000234","name":"Quick-Access Cut — Tailoring — Universal","type":"text","sort":23400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Quick-Access Cut</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Once per round draw one accessible light object as part of the action that uses it. Also secure two additional light objects against accidental loss. Does not reduce the use action&#39;s cost.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000235","name":"Layered Lining — Tailoring — Universal","type":"text","sort":23500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Layered Lining</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Universal</p><p>Garment supports two paid secondary textile or leather components without additional empty-lining Bulk. Materials and Marks still cost normally; this grants no Capacity or duplicate Core progression.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000236","name":"Combat Cut — Tailoring — Battlestitching","type":"text","sort":23600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Combat Cut</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Acrobatics checks to Tumble Through. It does not change movement cost or negate reactions from a failed check.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000237","name":"Quickdraw Harness — Tailoring — Battlestitching","type":"text","sort":23700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Quickdraw Harness</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Free action once per round: draw up to two weapons secured to this harness, provided you have enough free hands. It does not make a Strike or reduce other activation costs.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000238","name":"Vital Reinforcement — Tailoring — Battlestitching","type":"text","sort":23800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Vital Reinforcement</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Worn armor grants +18 × Core Tier maximum HP. This is maximum HP, not temporary HP or healing; repeated equipping must not restore damage.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000239","name":"Reactive Weave — Tailoring — Battlestitching","type":"text","sort":23900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reactive Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Reaction once per round when damaged: reduce that damage instance by 6 × Core Tier, or 10 × Core Tier if caused by a critical hit, minimum 0. This is reduction of one instance, not resistance for the round.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000240","name":"Duelist's War-Skin — Tailoring — Battlestitching","type":"text","sort":24000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Duelist&#39;s War-Skin</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Worn armor grants Artisan Bonuses of Core Tier to AC and Reflex saves, and 5 × Core Tier feet to land Speed. It grants no physical resistance.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000241","name":"War-Skin Regeneration — Tailoring — Battlestitching","type":"text","sort":24100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>War-Skin Regeneration</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Battlestitching</p><p>Worn armor grants +24 × Core Tier maximum HP. Once per day after an encounter, spend 10 minutes adjusting it to restore 8 × Core Tier HP. Replaces per-turn temporary HP and cannot heal through repeated equipping.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000242","name":"Silent Stitch — Tailoring — Veilcraft","type":"text","sort":24200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Silent Stitch</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Stealth checks where clothing noise matters. Enable the Mark condition only when muffling the garment would help.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000243","name":"Chameleon Cloth — Tailoring — Veilcraft","type":"text","sort":24300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Chameleon Cloth</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth checks to Hide or Sneak in one recorded environment palette. Enable the Mark condition only there; no half-Speed requirement beyond normal Sneak rules.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000244","name":"Many-Faced Weave — Tailoring — Veilcraft","type":"text","sort":24400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Many-Faced Weave</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>One minute of adjustment creates a recorded mundane disguise of clothing and facial framing. Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to Deception checks to Impersonate that identity. No size change or copied abilities; close examination still permits detection.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000245","name":"Shadow Mantle — Tailoring — Veilcraft","type":"text","sort":24500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Shadow Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>One action once per encounter for 1 minute: gain concealed in dim light or darkness and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth there. Attacking does not end concealment, but bright light suppresses it until you leave that light.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000246","name":"Phase Veil — Tailoring — Veilcraft","type":"text","sort":24600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Phase Veil</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>One action once per encounter until the end of your next turn: move through creature spaces and non-magical difficult terrain, gaining physical resistance equal to 6 × Core Tier. You cannot cross solid walls and must end movement in open space.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000247","name":"Null Mantle — Tailoring — Veilcraft","type":"text","sort":24700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Null Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Veilcraft</p><p>One action once per day for 1 minute: become invisible and gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves against magical detection. Hostile actions suppress invisibility until the start of your next turn. Does not negate precise non-visual senses.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000248","name":"Court Finish — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","type":"text","sort":24800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Court Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society checks involving formal protocol or heraldry. Enable the Mark condition only for those subjects.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000249","name":"Envoy's Raiment — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","type":"text","sort":24900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Envoy&#39;s Raiment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Diplomacy checks when acting in an officially recognised capacity. Enable the Mark condition only with a relevant mandate; social consequences still apply. Envoy&#39;s Reprise — Free action, once per day after failing a Diplomacy check made in your recognised official capacity: reroll and use the new result. This is a fortune effect; it cannot combine with another fortune effect on that roll.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Free Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000250","name":"Commander's Mantle — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","type":"text","sort":25000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Commander&#39;s Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Conscious wearer visibly leading allies grants those allies within 30 feet +5 Artisan Bonus to Aid checks and saves against fear. The wearer is not their own ally for this aura; record recipients manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000251","name":"Judicator's Robes — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","type":"text","sort":25100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Judicator&#39;s Robes</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to Perception checks to Sense Motive. One action once per encounter: designate a visible creature within 60 feet; allies gain +5 Artisan Bonus to their first save against it before the end of your next turn.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>1 Action</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000252","name":"Sovereign Presence — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","type":"text","sort":25200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sovereign Presence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Two actions once per encounter for 1 minute: allies within 30 feet gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves. Enemies within 30 feet take -3 Artisan Bonus to saves against your fear effects. This is a mental aura; unconsciousness ends it.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000253","name":"Coronation Regalia — Tailoring — Regaliacraft","type":"text","sort":25300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Coronation Regalia</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Tailoring — Regaliacraft</p><p>Worn armor grants its recognised office-holder +18 × Core Tier maximum HP and +5 Artisan Bonus to Diplomacy and Intimidation. Two actions once per day: allies within 30 feet gain a separately tracked 10-point Artisan temporary-HP buffer for 10 minutes. Do not overwrite class temporary HP; track and deduct this buffer manually.</p><p><em>High-power campaign revision. Flat Artisan bonuses stack. Structure and project benefits are descriptive; activations, recipients and limited uses require manual resolution unless the Workbench explicitly lists numerical automation. Additional temporary HP is tracked separately from class temporary HP.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>Armor</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>2 Actions</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>Superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>lining, backing, wrap, cover, core</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
